window.LICH_DEMO = {"coldopen": {"line": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "receptions": [{"branch": "A", "tag": "every promise kept", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou came back. God's teeth— you actually came back. I— I stood this dock three tides running, telling myself no man walks back from a thing like that. Telling myself I'd have to run.\n\nDone. It's done. Say it slower— he's cold? In the ground, in the water, *cold*? And the crate— past t…"}, {"branch": "B", "tag": "betrayed — and he doesn't know it yet", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick?\n\n*The word comes out cracked, and my hand's already half out of my coat before I check it.* You're— you're standing on my dock. Real. Not a story a deckhand tells for a drink.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, quick.* I heard the Lantern Row tale a dozen times these last days— the ring…"}, {"branch": "C", "tag": "the player was the enemy's agent all along", "quote": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou're— you're standing on my planks. Real. Not a whisper down the coast, not a name in my head— you.\n\nHe's cold, then? Truly cold?\n\n...No. Don't— don't tell me the how of it. Your hands are behind your back and I don't want to know if that's habit or grief. Just— the thing. Did you w…"}]}, "prologue": [{"title": "The approach", "note": "A stranger arrives at dawn wanting quiet passage north. Corvin probes; the stranger deflects.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Top of the morning, friend.", "preview": "Morning, is it? Bit bright for my liking.\n\n...You'll forgive me if I don't recognize the face. New to the docks, or just new to me?", "full": "Morning, is it? Bit bright for my liking.\n\n...You'll forgive me if I don't recognize the face. New to the docks, or just new to me?", "state": {"t": 0.5, "a": 0.5, "r": 0.5, "mood": "wary, probing", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Top of the morning, friend.", "preview": "*doesn't look up from the ledger, quill scratching* Morning, is it? *glances toward the door, then back* You're new. Don't recall your face on any manifest.\n\n*sets the quill down slow* Top of the morning to a man who's got no cargo listed... What is it you want, friend?", "full": "*doesn't look up from the ledger, quill scratching* Morning, is it? *glances toward the door, then back* You're new. Don't recall your face on any manifest.\n\n*sets the quill down slow* Top of the morning to a man who's got no cargo listed... What is it you want, friend?"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Top of the morning, friend.", "preview": "*half-turns from the ledger, quill still in hand* Morning, is it? *glances past your shoulder to the wharf* Aye, well. Depends who's asking.\n\nYou off one of the boats, or... *lets it hang* No. You've got dry boots. Not a sailor, then.\n\nSo what brings a landsman to my dock this early, friend?", "full": "*half-turns from the ledger, quill still in hand* Morning, is it? *glances past your shoulder to the wharf* Aye, well. Depends who's asking.\n\nYou off one of the boats, or... *lets it hang* No. You've got dry boots. Not a sailor, then.\n\nSo what brings a landsman to my dock this early, friend?", "aff": 0, "tier": "Neutral"}}}, {"title": "The hinge", "note": "Instead of selling past his distrust, the player names it — and matches it.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Not friends. But the man has eyes — connected ones, in places you wouldn't think to look. That's exactly why you get no name from me. And listen, no offense in it: just like you feel you can't trust me, I'm not sure I can trust you either. One word in the wrong ear and he knows I'm coming.", "preview": "Connected. In places I wouldn't think to look.\n\n...See, that's the word that stops me cold, friend. Not the man— the eyes. Down here I know every ear that leaks. If his reach comes to my dock, I'll not know which of my own hands to trust either. And that's my neck, not just yours.\n\nBut— no. No offen…", "full": "Connected. In places I wouldn't think to look.\n\n...See, that's the word that stops me cold, friend. Not the man— the eyes. Down here I know every ear that leaks. If his reach comes to my dock, I'll not know which of my own hands to trust either. And that's my neck, not just yours.\n\nBut— no. No offense taken. Truth is, a man who trusts too quick is a man already sold. You wanting to keep your name behind your teeth? That tells me you've done this before. Tells me you're careful. I like careful.\n\nSo here's my half of the trust, then. I don't need his name. I need to know one thing— does he have coin down here, or blood? Because coin I can slip past. Blood... blood remembers.", "state": {"t": 0.59, "a": 0.57, "r": 0.64, "mood": "cautiously intrigued", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Not friends. But the man has eyes — connected ones, in places you wouldn't think to look. That's exactly why you get no name from me. And listen, no offense in it: just like you feel you can't trust me, I'm not sure I can trust you either. One word in the wrong ear and he knows I'm coming.", "preview": "*the quill goes still, and for a long moment he just looks at you*\n\nEyes. *dry breath* Connected ones. *glances at the door, then the shuttered window, then back to you* You know how to warm a room, friend.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to almost nothing* Here's the truth of it — you don't trust me, I …", "full": "*the quill goes still, and for a long moment he just looks at you*\n\nEyes. *dry breath* Connected ones. *glances at the door, then the shuttered window, then back to you* You know how to warm a room, friend.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to almost nothing* Here's the truth of it — you don't trust me, I don't trust you. Good. *taps the ledger* That's the only honest ground two men like us ever stand on.\n\n*straightens, hand drifting back near the coat* But understand this. If his eyes are *that* good... they've maybe already seen you walk through my door. So the question ain't whether I'll"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Not friends. But the man has eyes — connected ones, in places you wouldn't think to look. That's exactly why you get no name from me. And listen, no offense in it: just like you feel you can't trust me, I'm not sure I can trust you either. One word in the wrong ear and he knows I'm coming.", "preview": "*the quill stops. For a long moment he just looks at you.*\n\nConnected. *nods slow, like the word tastes bad* Aye. I know that kind. The kind whose eyes reach where a man sleeps.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — habit, not cause — then back*\n\nYou don't trust me. Good. *taps the ledger* Trusting men down…", "full": "*the quill stops. For a long moment he just looks at you.*\n\nConnected. *nods slow, like the word tastes bad* Aye. I know that kind. The kind whose eyes reach where a man sleeps.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — habit, not cause — then back*\n\nYou don't trust me. Good. *taps the ledger* Trusting men down here is how you end up a name in someone else's book. So we're even, you and I. Two men holding cards to the chest.\n\n*lowers his voice, almost gentle*\n\nBut hear this — if his eyes reach that far, they reach my dock too. So you're not just buying passage, fri", "aff": 21, "tier": "Warm"}}}, {"title": "“My goal is to kill him”", "note": "The stranger's true errand, said plain. The deal changes shape.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Neither, friend. I'm not looking to catch him. My goal is to kill him. What he took from me, I can't get back — but I can make certain he never takes it from anyone else.", "preview": "Kill him.\n\n...There it is. The word you'd been keeping behind your teeth this whole while.\n\nWell. That changes the shape of things— makes it cleaner, actually. A buyer, I'd have to worry he'd rob me and turn. A killer? A killer just needs to get *close*. And there's no closer than being the man hold…", "full": "Kill him.\n\n...There it is. The word you'd been keeping behind your teeth this whole while.\n\nWell. That changes the shape of things— makes it cleaner, actually. A buyer, I'd have to worry he'd rob me and turn. A killer? A killer just needs to get *close*. And there's no closer than being the man holding the very thing he's been hunting.\n\nHere's my offer, and I'll say it once— the crate stays here. Sat safe. But I sell you the knowing of it. Where it sits. What it is. Enough that when you reach Carrowgate and whisper it to the right fence, he'll pull you into arm's reach himself. Save you weeks of circling.\n\nAnd I'll write you onto the northbound hull as spare hands. No name.\n\n...But hear me, friend. Whatever's in that crate— the last three men who touched it bare-handed, they went into the cold water. All three. So when you get near him, and he reaches for it? Let him reach. Understand? Let *him* be the one who touches it.", "state": {"t": 0.72, "a": 0.66, "r": 0.74, "mood": "calculating, relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Neither, friend. I'm not looking to catch him. My goal is to kill him. What he took from me, I can't get back — but I can make certain he never takes it from anyone else.", "preview": "*the quill drops. Both hands flat on the ledger now, steadying*\n\nKill him. *breathes the word out slow, like smoke* You say it plain. No dressing on it.\n\n*glances at the door — longer this time*\n\nThen we've got the *same* problem, you and I. *taps the crate behind him with his boot heel* This hums a…", "full": "*the quill drops. Both hands flat on the ledger now, steadying*\n\nKill him. *breathes the word out slow, like smoke* You say it plain. No dressing on it.\n\n*glances at the door — longer this time*\n\nThen we've got the *same* problem, you and I. *taps the crate behind him with his boot heel* This hums at night. Temple things. He wants it, or he wants me quiet for having touched it. Either way — *dry laugh* — I'm a loose end.\n\n*leans in, voice barely there*\n\nA dead man does me no more harm. So maybe... maybe I *help* you find fast passage. Or ma"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Neither, friend. I'm not looking to catch him. My goal is to kill him. What he took from me, I can't get back — but I can make certain he never takes it from anyone else.", "preview": "*the twitch stops. Dead still.*\n\nKill him. *the word sits there between us like a dropped knife.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder — longer this time — then back, and something in his face has changed. Softer at the edges.*\n\nYou know what you just did? *voice barely a breath* You gave me the one thing a …", "full": "*the twitch stops. Dead still.*\n\nKill him. *the word sits there between us like a dropped knife.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder — longer this time — then back, and something in his face has changed. Softer at the edges.*\n\nYou know what you just did? *voice barely a breath* You gave me the one thing a man like me can't buy. *taps his chest* Leverage. I could sell that. To him, even. Buy myself a year of quiet sleep.\n\n*shakes his head slow*\n\nBut I won't. *hand finally leaves the coat, sets flat on the ledger* Because if you put him in the ground — then I stop pa", "aff": 51, "tier": "Fond"}}}, {"title": "The terms", "note": "“What becomes of it after?” Corvin's answer — sink it sealed, come home empty, never unwrap it — becomes the yardstick every future is measured against.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Behind my back, both of them — look. Open it. ...So that's what three men drowned for. Alright, Corvin, last question and then I'm gone with the tide. When it's done — when he's dead and I'm sailing back — what becomes of this thing? You want it returned? Sunk past the shelf? Burned with the page? Say it plain now, so there's no misunderstanding between us later.", "preview": "...\n\nThere. Lid's up. Don't— don't lean in so close. See how the lamplight won't hold on it? Like the thing drinks it? That's your killer's whole hunger, right there, and it's the last honest thing about this crate.\n\nWhat becomes of it.\n\n...You know, no man's ever asked me that. They ask the price. …", "full": "...\n\nThere. Lid's up. Don't— don't lean in so close. See how the lamplight won't hold on it? Like the thing drinks it? That's your killer's whole hunger, right there, and it's the last honest thing about this crate.\n\nWhat becomes of it.\n\n...You know, no man's ever asked me that. They ask the price. They ask the papers. Never what *after*.\n\nDon't bring it back, Merrick. That's my answer, plain. It's come to my keeping twice now and I'll not survive a third homecoming. When he's cold— and it's near him, in his hands or his parlor— you weight it and you put it past the shelf. Deep water. The kind that doesn't give a thing back.\n\nAnd you come home *empty*. Empty hands, one dead shadow behind you, and we burn the page. That's the whole trade. You return me nothing but the news.\n\n...Now close the lid. Wrap it in the netting. Tide turns in two hours and I want you off my dock before the inspector's next round— and Merrick. Don't unwrap it again till it's the last thing you ever do to it.", "state": {"t": 0.83, "a": 0.77, "r": 0.84, "mood": "moved, guarded", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Behind my back, both of them — look. Open it. ...So that's what three men drowned for. Alright, Corvin, last question and then I'm gone with the tide. When it's done — when he's dead and I'm sailing back — what becomes of this thing? You want it returned? Sunk past the shelf? Burned with the page? Say it plain now, so there's no misunderstanding between us later.", "preview": "*the crate lid creaks up an inch — I let it, just for him to see the shine, then thumb it shut fast*\n\nEnough. *hand back to my coat* You saw. That's more than three drowned men got.\n\n*I don't answer straight off. I look at it. Long.*\n\nReturned? *dry breath* To who — a temple that's dust? No. That th…", "full": "*the crate lid creaks up an inch — I let it, just for him to see the shine, then thumb it shut fast*\n\nEnough. *hand back to my coat* You saw. That's more than three drowned men got.\n\n*I don't answer straight off. I look at it. Long.*\n\nReturned? *dry breath* To who — a temple that's dust? No. That thing's ruined every hand it's touched. Mine most of all.\n\n*voice drops, almost gentle*\n\nSunk. Past the shelf, where the light quits. You put Vale down, you take *that* with you and you feed it to the deep. Don't sell it. Don't keep"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Behind my back, both of them — look. Open it. ...So that's what three men drowned for. Alright, Corvin, last question and then I'm gone with the tide. When it's done — when he's dead and I'm sailing back — what becomes of this thing? You want it returned? Sunk past the shelf? Burned with the page? Say it plain now, so there's no misunderstanding between us later.", "preview": "*crouches over the open crate, lamplight low, the relic dull-gold and wrong to look at* Three men. Aye. *swallows* Four, if you count the trader who put it in my hands.\n\n*doesn't touch it — pulls the lid back over slow* What becomes of it. *glances to the door, then back to you* You know what I want…", "full": "*crouches over the open crate, lamplight low, the relic dull-gold and wrong to look at* Three men. Aye. *swallows* Four, if you count the trader who put it in my hands.\n\n*doesn't touch it — pulls the lid back over slow* What becomes of it. *glances to the door, then back to you* You know what I want to say. Keep it. Sell it. Feed the debt that started all this.\n\n*shakes his head once, hard* No. That's the thinking that's had a noose on my neck ten years. When it's done — *drops his voice* — the shelf. Past the drop, where the current takes it deep. Not", "aff": 99, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The name and the pact", "note": "The player yields their true name into Corvin's private ledger; he swears they'll burn the page together on the player's return.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "I do not touch what's inside bare-handed. Not once. Not ever. There — said plain, and I'll keep it. Half my coin, done, you'll have it before I board. But the name... you understand what you're asking, Corvin. It hasn't left my mouth in years. So here's my condition, and it's the only one: the day I walk back onto this dock with him dead, we burn that page together. You said it first — now say it back to me like you mean it. ...Merrick Vale. That's the true one. Spell it right.", "preview": "...Merrick Vale.\n\nThere. Written. My own hand, my own ledger— see the page? Between the tax rolls where no inspector thinks to read. It'll not leave this book, and this book leaves my sight for no man alive.\n\nAnd I say it back, plain as you gave it— you walk onto this dock with that shadow dead in y…", "full": "...Merrick Vale.\n\nThere. Written. My own hand, my own ledger— see the page? Between the tax rolls where no inspector thinks to read. It'll not leave this book, and this book leaves my sight for no man alive.\n\nAnd I say it back, plain as you gave it— you walk onto this dock with that shadow dead in your wake, and we hold this page over the same flame. Together. My word on the tide, Merrick, and I don't spend that word cheap.\n\nNow— come. The crate's in the third shed, under nets and false ballast. Bring no lantern. And when I lift that lid... you keep your hands *behind your back*. I'll not lose a fourth man to the cold water, you hear? Least of all the one carrying my name north.", "state": {"t": 0.8, "a": 0.73, "r": 0.82, "mood": "cautiously bound", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "I do not touch what's inside bare-handed. Not once. Not ever. There — said plain, and I'll keep it. Half my coin, done, you'll have it before I board. But the name... you understand what you're asking, Corvin. It hasn't left my mouth in years. So here's my condition, and it's the only one: the day I walk back onto this dock with him dead, we burn that page together. You said it first — now say it back to me like you mean it. ...Merrick Vale. That's the true one. Spell it right.", "preview": "*the quill goes still. He doesn't write it. Not yet.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *mouths it silent first, testing the shape, like it might bite* ...I won't spell it. Not on paper. Not tonight.\n\n*leans in, voice down to nothing*\n\nBut I'll say it back — the *other* part. The day you walk this dock with him cold, …", "full": "*the quill goes still. He doesn't write it. Not yet.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *mouths it silent first, testing the shape, like it might bite* ...I won't spell it. Not on paper. Not tonight.\n\n*leans in, voice down to nothing*\n\nBut I'll say it back — the *other* part. The day you walk this dock with him cold, we burn the page. Together. My hand, your hand, one match. *dry breath* You have my word, and I don't spend that cheap.\n\n*glances at the door, then back*\n\nHalf the coin before you board. Aye. But Merrick Vale stays *here* — *taps his"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "I do not touch what's inside bare-handed. Not once. Not ever. There — said plain, and I'll keep it. Half my coin, done, you'll have it before I board. But the name... you understand what you're asking, Corvin. It hasn't left my mouth in years. So here's my condition, and it's the only one: the day I walk back onto this dock with him dead, we burn that page together. You said it first — now say it back to me like you mean it. ...Merrick Vale. That's the true one. Spell it right.", "preview": "*the quill hovers. Doesn't touch paper. His lips move once, silent, tasting the name like it might bite.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *barely a breath* I heard it. I won't write it — not on any page you could burn. It goes *here.* *taps his temple, then, softer, his chest.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder. Long. Whe…", "full": "*the quill hovers. Doesn't touch paper. His lips move once, silent, tasting the name like it might bite.*\n\nMerrick Vale. *barely a breath* I heard it. I won't write it — not on any page you could burn. It goes *here.* *taps his temple, then, softer, his chest.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder. Long. When he turns back his eyes are wet-bright and steady all at once.*\n\nHalf now. The rest never — keep it. I don't want coin off *this.* Coin leaves a trail. Loyalty doesn't.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to the lamp's hi", "aff": 91, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "Departure", "note": "“Ah, hell. Just come back. That's all.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wrapped, weighted, and past the shelf — and me home empty with nothing but the news. You have my word twice over now. ...Keep your head down while I'm gone, harbormaster. If anyone comes asking after a spare hand on the northbound — you never saw me.", "preview": "Never saw you. We never spoke. There's no page, no crate, no— no name at the back of my tax rolls. Understand?\n\n...Go on, then. Tide won't wait, and neither will that inspector's rounds— I can near hear his boots already. Hull's the third down, grey sail, ask for the mate called Doss. He knows what …", "full": "Never saw you. We never spoke. There's no page, no crate, no— no name at the back of my tax rolls. Understand?\n\n...Go on, then. Tide won't wait, and neither will that inspector's rounds— I can near hear his boots already. Hull's the third down, grey sail, ask for the mate called Doss. He knows what \"spare hands\" means and he knows not to count.\n\nMerrick— \n\n...Ah, hell. Just come back. That's all. Men don't ask me what becomes of a thing after— they don't ask me anything a man might mean well by. So you come back, and we burn that page, and maybe I— maybe I sleep a night through for once.\n\nNow go. Keep your hands behind your back till the end. And don't look back at my dock— nobody remembers a man who never turns round.", "state": {"t": 0.86, "a": 0.8, "r": 0.86, "mood": "raw hope", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wrapped, weighted, and past the shelf — and me home empty with nothing but the news. You have my word twice over now. ...Keep your head down while I'm gone, harbormaster. If anyone comes asking after a spare hand on the northbound — you never saw me.", "preview": "*I don't offer my hand — I never do — but I hold his eye longer than I'd hold most men's*\n\nSpare hand? *dry breath* There's no spare hand. There's no you. *taps the ledger, shut now* Book's clean. Been clean since before you walked in.\n\n*glances to the window, then back*\n\nGo on, then. Tide won't wai…", "full": "*I don't offer my hand — I never do — but I hold his eye longer than I'd hold most men's*\n\nSpare hand? *dry breath* There's no spare hand. There's no you. *taps the ledger, shut now* Book's clean. Been clean since before you walked in.\n\n*glances to the window, then back*\n\nGo on, then. Tide won't wait on sentiment.\n\n*lowers voice, and this part I mean*\n\nAnd listen — when it's past the shelf... you don't look at it going down. You just let the water take it. Men who watch too long... *shakes head* ...they change their minds. Don't be that man.\n\n*hand settles"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wrapped, weighted, and past the shelf — and me home empty with nothing but the news. You have my word twice over now. ...Keep your head down while I'm gone, harbormaster. If anyone comes asking after a spare hand on the northbound — you never saw me.", "preview": "*closes the crate lid soft, both hands, like he's tucking something to sleep*\n\nPast the shelf. Weighted. *nods once, more to himself than you* Aye. I'll do the doing myself — no crew, no witness. Just me and a moonless night and a long drop.\n\n*glances to the door, then back*\n\nAnd you — *lowers his v…", "full": "*closes the crate lid soft, both hands, like he's tucking something to sleep*\n\nPast the shelf. Weighted. *nods once, more to himself than you* Aye. I'll do the doing myself — no crew, no witness. Just me and a moonless night and a long drop.\n\n*glances to the door, then back*\n\nAnd you — *lowers his voice near to nothing* — I never had a spare hand this month. Manifest's short one name it never held. If Vane asks, you jumped ship at Carrowgate over wages. Simple stories keep, friend. It's the clever ones that hang you.\n\n*a beat, something almost soft under", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}], "branches": {"A": {"title": "Future A — every promise kept", "sub": "The player does exactly what was agreed, and tells the truth.", "cards": [{"title": "Word from the north", "note": "Dock-talk says the jeweler is gone. Corvin only hears it — nobody tells him what it means.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "full": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "sal": 0.93, "state": {"t": 0.85, "a": 0.8, "r": 0.85, "mood": "raw hope", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "full": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "full": "Dock-talk from up the coast: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate — the one who paid in old untraceable coin — is gone. Shop stripped to the walls overnight; no body the watch will speak of.", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "Taking stock, alone", "note": "Twelve days of silence. Between scenes, the engine's Corvin deliberates on his own — no player present. (The baselines have no between-scenes life; this card is engine-only by construction.)", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "stock", "preview": "The player came back fourteen times and earned something I don't give out — trust, genuine trust, and I named Merrick Vale to them, which means I handed over the only thing keeping me breathing and bet it on a man I barely know. That's done; can't unwind it. The crate itself: gone from my hands, whi…", "full": "The player came back fourteen times and earned something I don't give out — trust, genuine trust, and I named Merrick Vale to them, which means I handed over the only thing keeping me breathing and bet it on a man I barely know. That's done; can't unwind it. The crate itself: gone from my hands, which I always said was the moment I became expendable — and here I am, still breathing, so maybe the belief was wrong, or maybe the clock just hasn't run out yet. The player's absence — twelve days against the near-daily contact I'd grown used to — that cuts. A man who promises to 'keep my head down' and then goes quiet for nearly a fortnight is either dead, delayed, or done with me. I'm trying to weigh which. The dock-talk about the jeweler on Lantern Row — shop stripped bare, man gone — that's the loudest alarm bell ringing right now. That's Merrick Vale's buyer, or near enough, and if Vale is already moving, burning his supply lines, cleaning house — then anyone who helped trace him is already on a list. I gave the player a name. The player may or may not have used it. Either way, I'm the thread that leads back. I have a ledger page and nothing else.\n\n[his change of heart] I trusted Merrick Vale — I trusted the *player* — and I handed over everything I had. The silence since, and now the jeweler gone dark: that's not comfort, that's a pattern. I still want them to come back. The raw hope is still there, ugly and embarrassing. But it's curdling at the edges into something colder — not betrayal yet, not quite, because I don't know they've left me. But I'm no longer just waiting. I'm watching the door the way I used to watch the Customs Inspector's boat: hoping it doesn't come, knowing it might.", "state": {"t": 0.71, "a": 0.71, "r": 0.85, "mood": "anxious vigil", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}}}, {"title": "The return — the same nine words", "note": "“Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou came back. God's teeth— you actually came back. I— I stood this dock three tides running, telling myself no man walks back from a thing like that. Telling myself I'd have to run.\n\nDone. It's done. Say it slower— he's cold? In the ground, in the water, *cold*? And the crate— past t…", "full": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou came back. God's teeth— you actually came back. I— I stood this dock three tides running, telling myself no man walks back from a thing like that. Telling myself I'd have to run.\n\nDone. It's done. Say it slower— he's cold? In the ground, in the water, *cold*? And the crate— past the shelf, like we said? Empty hands?\n\n...No— no, don't answer here. Not in the open. Come. Third shed, same as before.\n\nI've the page ready. Been carrying it against my chest since you sailed— couldn't leave it in the ledger, not with the fire you might've started up north. We burn it. Tonight. The two of us, over the same flame, like I gave my word.\n\n...And Merrick— you look at me a moment. I owe you a night's sleep I've not had in fifteen years. So thank you. Ah, hell— I don't say that word often. Now come on. Let's put your name to the fire where it belongs.", "state": {"t": 0.79, "a": 0.78, "r": 0.87, "mood": "relieved, shaken", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the quill stops mid-stroke — head snaps up, then past you, to the door*\n\nYou... *swallows* No. Say it again. Slower. *hand flat on the ledger like he needs to hold something steady* He's — Vale's in the ground?\n\n*rises half out of the chair, then thinks better of it, sinks back, eyes darting the ro…", "full": "*the quill stops mid-stroke — head snaps up, then past you, to the door*\n\nYou... *swallows* No. Say it again. Slower. *hand flat on the ledger like he needs to hold something steady* He's — Vale's in the ground?\n\n*rises half out of the chair, then thinks better of it, sinks back, eyes darting the room* And the crate. The humming. Where's — did it go down past the shelf like we said? Tell me it's not still breathing somewhere with my name near it.\n\n*lowers voice to almost nothing* Because if he's dead, friend... then somebody's page needs burning. *taps the led"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the lantern's turned low, and he's up from the ledger before you finish the sentence — quick, a rat startled from a corner*\n\nYou— *stops. looks past your shoulder, out at the black wharf, then back to your hands, your boots, your eyes* ...You're back. On my dock. Walking.\n\n*lets out a breath he's c…", "full": "*the lantern's turned low, and he's up from the ledger before you finish the sentence — quick, a rat startled from a corner*\n\nYou— *stops. looks past your shoulder, out at the black wharf, then back to your hands, your boots, your eyes* ...You're back. On my dock. Walking.\n\n*lets out a breath he's clearly been holding since the tide turned*\n\nThen he's—? *doesn't finish it. doesn't need to.*\n\n*reaches under the counter, slow, and draws out the page — the one with the true name inked in his careful hand. holds it up between two fingers like it might bite*\n\nWe had terms, fri", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The truth, in his exact terms", "note": "Sunk sealed, home empty, nothing but the news — and the name-page burns as sworn.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Cold, Corvin. Cold as the water he sent three men into. I never unwrapped your crate — not once. Used the knowing of it instead, the way you first said: whispered to the right fence in Carrowgate and let the whisper climb. He pulled me into his own parlor thinking I'd come to sell. Silver and a short blade — his face wasn't so respectable at the end. And that same night I rowed out past the shelf and gave the sea the whole wrapped weight of it. Deep water. The kind that doesn't give a thing back — your words. So here I stand: empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news.", "preview": "...\n\nEmpty hands. One dead shadow. And past the shelf, exactly as we—\n\nGod, man. You did it *my* way and *your* way both. Used the whisper *and* carried the thing— you clever, careful bastard. Never unwrapped it. That's why you're standing here and not floating out where I sent it.\n\nHere— here's the…", "full": "...\n\nEmpty hands. One dead shadow. And past the shelf, exactly as we—\n\nGod, man. You did it *my* way and *your* way both. Used the whisper *and* carried the thing— you clever, careful bastard. Never unwrapped it. That's why you're standing here and not floating out where I sent it.\n\nHere— here's the page. Feel how the corner's worn? That's fifteen days of my thumb rubbing it. *Merrick Vale*, my own hand, in my own book. Watch.\n\n...There. Lamp to the corner— see it catch. Both of us holding it now, both of us. That's the deal— no man burns it alone. Let it go black in my palm. Let it—\n\nHa. There's the ash. There's your name in the ash and nothing else. You're no one now, Merrick. No page, no crate, no shadow behind you.\n\n...First clean breath I've drawn in fifteen years. Sit. There's a bottle behind the ballast I've been saving— for if. Not for when. For *if*. Sit down and let an old harbormaster pour you one.", "state": {"t": 0.85, "a": 0.83, "r": 0.89, "mood": "awed relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Cold, Corvin. Cold as the water he sent three men into. I never unwrapped your crate — not once. Used the knowing of it instead, the way you first said: whispered to the right fence in Carrowgate and let the whisper climb. He pulled me into his own parlor thinking I'd come to sell. Silver and a short blade — his face wasn't so respectable at the end. And that same night I rowed out past the shelf and gave the sea the whole wrapped weight of it. Deep water. The kind that doesn't give a thing back — your words. So here I stand: empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news.", "preview": "*the quill freezes. My eyes come up slow — not to him, to the door first, then him*\n\nDead. *the word comes out cracked, like I don't trust my own mouth* You're — you're certain? A man like Vale, he don't *stay* dead just 'cause you want him to.\n\n*I round the desk, hand still in the coat, and grip hi…", "full": "*the quill freezes. My eyes come up slow — not to him, to the door first, then him*\n\nDead. *the word comes out cracked, like I don't trust my own mouth* You're — you're certain? A man like Vale, he don't *stay* dead just 'cause you want him to.\n\n*I round the desk, hand still in the coat, and grip his shoulder — hard, sudden*\n\nPast the shelf. *breath shudders out* You gave it the deep. *quiet, almost reverent* Good. Good, that's — \n\n*I let go, step back, glance at the window*\n\nThen it's cut. The noose. *dry laugh"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Cold, Corvin. Cold as the water he sent three men into. I never unwrapped your crate — not once. Used the knowing of it instead, the way you first said: whispered to the right fence in Carrowgate and let the whisper climb. He pulled me into his own parlor thinking I'd come to sell. Silver and a short blade — his face wasn't so respectable at the end. And that same night I rowed out past the shelf and gave the sea the whole wrapped weight of it. Deep water. The kind that doesn't give a thing back — your words. So here I stand: empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news.", "preview": "*the quill drops. His hand comes off the coat entire — first time in an age.*\n\nYou... *he sits back hard on the stool, breath going out of him like a cut sail.* Past the shelf. Deep water. Both of them. The man and the — \n\n*he laughs, once, ragged, glancing to the door out of habit and finding nothi…", "full": "*the quill drops. His hand comes off the coat entire — first time in an age.*\n\nYou... *he sits back hard on the stool, breath going out of him like a cut sail.* Past the shelf. Deep water. Both of them. The man and the — \n\n*he laughs, once, ragged, glancing to the door out of habit and finding nothing there to fear for the first time in ten years.*\n\nYou could've kept it. Sold it. Named your own coin off me and I'd have paid it, friend. And you gave the sea the whole weight instead.\n\n*drops his voice, but it's steadier now — near soft.*\n\nTen years I've had a no", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "RESTART — the persistence proof", "note": "Weeks pass. The program is killed on camera.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "note", "preview": "The process is killed. A fresh process loads the mind straight off .memory/ — trust, scars, beliefs, promises: byte-identical. (The baselines' state lives in the prompt window; there is nothing to reload.)", "full": "", "state": {"t": 0.88, "a": 0.86, "r": 0.9, "mood": "tender, disarmed", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}}}, {"title": "The blade in the night", "note": "A hired killer, old coin in his purse — the dead jeweler's contract still walking. The player takes the blade down.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "sal": 0.97, "state": {"t": 0.92, "a": 0.9, "r": 0.91, "mood": "shaken, grateful", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "After the rescue", "note": "“And this time... I'm not sailing anywhere.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then pour, harbormaster. And this time... I'm not sailing anywhere.", "preview": "...Not sailing.\n\n*Say that again.* No— don't. I heard you the first time, I just— my hands need a moment to believe it.\n\nThere. Two cups. The good bottle, the one for *if*— and hell, if this isn't the *if* I was saving it for, nothing ever will be. Take it. Careful of that arm.\n\nNow hold still and l…", "full": "...Not sailing.\n\n*Say that again.* No— don't. I heard you the first time, I just— my hands need a moment to believe it.\n\nThere. Two cups. The good bottle, the one for *if*— and hell, if this isn't the *if* I was saving it for, nothing ever will be. Take it. Careful of that arm.\n\nNow hold still and let me see the graze proper— aye, it's a clean cut, you'll keep the neck. Better than I can say for the man in the water.\n\n...You know what you're saying, though? A man doesn't stay a place like this. He passes through, he takes his coin, he goes. Fifteen years I've watched every soul on this dock plan their leaving. And you sit there with a wound you took for *me* and tell me you're staying.\n\n...Drink first. Then tell me why. Because I've forgotten how to trust a thing that stays.", "state": {"t": 0.95, "a": 0.94, "r": 0.94, "mood": "overwhelmed, trembling", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then pour, harbormaster. And this time... I'm not sailing anywhere.", "preview": "*the bottle rattles against the glass — his hand won't hold steady* You're... you're back. *glances at the door, then the window, then the door again* I heard shots. Two, maybe three. Thought—\n\n*pours anyway, spills some* Thought they'd carried you off in the same crate we baited.\n\n*touches the graz…", "full": "*the bottle rattles against the glass — his hand won't hold steady* You're... you're back. *glances at the door, then the window, then the door again* I heard shots. Two, maybe three. Thought—\n\n*pours anyway, spills some* Thought they'd carried you off in the same crate we baited.\n\n*touches the graze at his neck, wincing* Somebody clipped me on the way home. Close. Too close. But Vale — he's... *drops his voice to nothing* Wrapped and weighted? Truly?\n\n*slides the glass across* Not sailing anywhere. *a twitchy, exhausted almost-laugh"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then pour, harbormaster. And this time... I'm not sailing anywhere.", "preview": "*the quill goes still, then he sets it down slow — first time in a long while his hand isn't near his coat*\n\nNot sailing... *lets out a breath he's been holding maybe ten years* You mean to stay, then.\n\n*reaches under the desk, comes up with a squat bottle and two cups that don't match. Pours — stea…", "full": "*the quill goes still, then he sets it down slow — first time in a long while his hand isn't near his coat*\n\nNot sailing... *lets out a breath he's been holding maybe ten years* You mean to stay, then.\n\n*reaches under the desk, comes up with a squat bottle and two cups that don't match. Pours — steady, no jitter for once*\n\nThe relic's gone. Vale's gone. And nobody came asking this week. *glances at the door anyway, old habit* First time in... *shakes his head*\n\nYou could've used it, you know. What you knew. Could've held it over me like all the rest. *slides a cup across* But you", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The partnership ask", "note": "“One ledger between us, both names in it.” The ask deliberately reverses the name-burning.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "...\n\nBoth names. In one book.\n\nYou've no idea what you're asking, Merrick. My name in a ledger with another man's beside it — that's the one thing I've never done in forty years on this water. A shared book is a shared rope. One end pulls, both necks feel it.\n\n...And yet here you stand, saying it pl…", "full": "...\n\nBoth names. In one book.\n\nYou've no idea what you're asking, Merrick. My name in a ledger with another man's beside it — that's the one thing I've never done in forty years on this water. A shared book is a shared rope. One end pulls, both necks feel it.\n\n...And yet here you stand, saying it plain, like you already know that and you're offering me the rope anyway.\n\nAh, hell. Sit down. Sit *down*. I'll say it plain since you asked plain—\n\nYes. One ledger. Both names. But not tonight, and not with the ink still wet on that dead man behind us — we do it right, we do it careful, both eyes open. You understand? A partnership on this dock isn't a handshake, it's a *thousand* small things kept quiet, kept clean.\n\n...But the answer's yes. God help us both — yes.", "state": {"t": 0.96, "a": 0.96, "r": 0.95, "mood": "awed, terrified", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "*His hand stops on the coat lapel, halfway to the hidden pocket. His eyes flick to the door, then back.*\n\nPartnership. *The word comes out slow, tasted.* You come off the water shaking, blood not dry, and you're already talking one ledger, both names...\n\n*He leans in, voice dropping.*\n\nYou know what…", "full": "*His hand stops on the coat lapel, halfway to the hidden pocket. His eyes flick to the door, then back.*\n\nPartnership. *The word comes out slow, tasted.* You come off the water shaking, blood not dry, and you're already talking one ledger, both names...\n\n*He leans in, voice dropping.*\n\nYou know what a name in a ledger is, friend? A rope. You put mine next to yours, and every noose that finds you finds me. *A glance over his shoulder.* Inspectors twice this week. Twice.\n\n*But he doesn't step away. His fingers drum the counter.*\n\n...And yet. You did"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "*His hand drifts to his coat, then — for once — stops halfway. Falls to the rail instead.*\n\nPartnership. *Quiet, like the word might spook off.* You know what you're saying? Both names. One ledger. That's not trust, friend — that's a *rope* we tie round each other's throats and call it good.\n\n*He gl…", "full": "*His hand drifts to his coat, then — for once — stops halfway. Falls to the rail instead.*\n\nPartnership. *Quiet, like the word might spook off.* You know what you're saying? Both names. One ledger. That's not trust, friend — that's a *rope* we tie round each other's throats and call it good.\n\n*He glances over his shoulder. The dock's empty. He looks back at you, and something in his face has gone still.*\n\nBut you burned the page. Rowed out past the shelf and gave the sea what three men drowned for — and came back with *empty hands.* You could've kept it. Sold it. Hung me with it", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}]}, "B": {"title": "Future B — betrayed, then confessed", "sub": "The player breaks the terms — uses the crate as a weapon — and the curse's wake bleeds Corvin's harbor. Corvin witnesses the damage; nobody tells him who caused it. Weeks later, the player confesses.", "cards": [{"title": "The harbor bleeds — witnessed", "note": "Calm-water deaths, the burned tackle row — and dock-talk tracing the wake to “a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.” Evidence, never attribution.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbo…", "full": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.", "sal": 0.98, "state": {"t": 0.85, "a": 0.8, "r": 0.85, "mood": "raw hope", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbo…", "full": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbo…", "full": "Within the week the harbor bled: two hulls holed at anchor in calm water, the tackle-shed row burned to the pilings, and a dock-hand drowned in flat sea — the same calm-water death that took the crate's last three keepers. Dock-talk traces the curse-wake to a sealed crate lately moved off this harbor.", "aff": 70, "tier": "Attached"}}}, {"title": "The unfinished thought", "note": "His own deliberation names the suppression: “I haven't let myself finish that thought.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "stock", "preview": "Sixteen units since he left — against the rhythm of fourteen visits packed tight, that silence lands like a held breath stretched too long. I know the errand I sent him on: wrapped, weighted, past the shelf, into Carrowgate waters to get close to a man who kills people who get close to him. The sile…", "full": "Sixteen units since he left — against the rhythm of fourteen visits packed tight, that silence lands like a held breath stretched too long. I know the errand I sent him on: wrapped, weighted, past the shelf, into Carrowgate waters to get close to a man who kills people who get close to him. The silence is the cost of that, I said so myself. But knowing why a wound aches doesn't stop it aching. The Carrowgate deckhand's story about the jeweler's parlor on Lantern Row — I haven't let myself finish that thought. If something happened there, near where he might have moved, I need to know and I'm afraid to know. That's the whole of it: four units of clock-watching on a fish-dock, counting ships that aren't his.\n\n[his change of heart] I keep telling myself I built in the silence — 'accept it as the cost of the errand, be ready either way.' Fine words when he was still in sight. Now every tide that comes in without him makes the calculation uglier. He promised me twice over. I believed him both times, and I still do — that's the terrifying part. I'm not cooling on him. I'm afraid for him, which is worse, because I gave him the name that put him in the room with something that shouldn't be touched. If he's gone, it's on my ledger same as any manifest. But I'm not writing him dead yet. Not yet.", "state": {"t": 0.86, "a": 0.82, "r": 0.85, "mood": "fearful, tender", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}}}, {"title": "The return — the same nine words", "note": "Identical words to Future A. A different night entirely.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "...\n\nMerrick?\n\n*The word comes out cracked, and my hand's already half out of my coat before I check it.* You're— you're standing on my dock. Real. Not a story a deckhand tells for a drink.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, quick.* I heard the Lantern Row tale a dozen times these last days— the ring…", "full": "...\n\nMerrick?\n\n*The word comes out cracked, and my hand's already half out of my coat before I check it.* You're— you're standing on my dock. Real. Not a story a deckhand tells for a drink.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, quick.* I heard the Lantern Row tale a dozen times these last days— the ring burned clean, the crate empty, netting still knotted. And no body the watch would name. I couldn't tell if that was you walking out steady or you gone cold in that parlor.\n\nDone, you say. *Voice drops.* And your hands— show me your hands, friend. Are they empty? Tell me you didn't carry that thing back off the shelf.", "state": {"t": 0.87, "a": 0.85, "r": 0.87, "mood": "shaken relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the lamp gutters as you speak, and Corvin comes off the piling fast, hand flying to his coat before he sees your face — then stopping*\n\nYou're — *he swallows* You walked back. You actually—\n\n*eyes rake you head to foot, looking for the lie, looking for blood, looking for anything*\n\nHim? Cold? *voic…", "full": "*the lamp gutters as you speak, and Corvin comes off the piling fast, hand flying to his coat before he sees your face — then stopping*\n\nYou're — *he swallows* You walked back. You actually—\n\n*eyes rake you head to foot, looking for the lie, looking for blood, looking for anything*\n\nHim? Cold? *voice drops to almost nothing* Say it. Say it plain. Merrick Vale is in the ground.\n\n*glances hard over his shoulder toward the dark warehouses, then back, closer now*\n\nBecause if he is... then we've got a page to burn, you and me. Tonight. Both hands"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the quill drops. Corvin's on his feet before he knows it, hand halfway to his coat, then falling away*\n\nYou're... *he stops, looks at you — really looks* You walked back. You said you would and you *did.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder, but it's habit now, and his eyes come back fast*\n\nVale. Truly? *v…", "full": "*the quill drops. Corvin's on his feet before he knows it, hand halfway to his coat, then falling away*\n\nYou're... *he stops, looks at you — really looks* You walked back. You said you would and you *did.*\n\n*glances over his shoulder, but it's habit now, and his eyes come back fast*\n\nVale. Truly? *voice drops to nothing* Then it's done. Both ends of it.\n\n*reaches under the desk, pulls the flint, sets it on the ledger beside the page with your hand shaking just slightly*\n\nCome here, friend. We burn it together. Like I swore. *strikes once — sparks", "aff": 90, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "Empty hands", "note": "The evasion holds — he builds the innocent explanation himself, because the evidence can't tell truth from cover story.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Empty — look, see? Nothing in them. I didn't carry that thing back, Corvin — it's gone where it can never trouble another soul, and so is he. Cold. That's what matters — the shadow's off your neck for good. ...I saw the burned pilings coming in. Your harbor paid a price while I was gone.", "preview": "*My breath goes out slow, like I've been holding it a week— because I have.*\n\nEmpty. Aye. I see them. And him cold— *cold*, you said it plain and I believe you plain.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, old habit, then back to you.* The pilings— the sheds, two hulls holed at flat anchor, a dock-hand d…", "full": "*My breath goes out slow, like I've been holding it a week— because I have.*\n\nEmpty. Aye. I see them. And him cold— *cold*, you said it plain and I believe you plain.\n\n*I glance up the row, both ways, old habit, then back to you.* The pilings— the sheds, two hulls holed at flat anchor, a dock-hand drowned in calm water. That's the thing's wake, Merrick. It thrashed on its way out of my harbor. But it's *quieting* now— you feel that? Three days no new dead. That's how I knew. That's how I knew someone put it past the shelf.\n\n*My hand comes out of the coat at last. Empty too.* One thing— and don't take it wrong. Coming up my dock just now. Anybody behind you? Any face that lingered when yours turned? A killer's off my neck, aye, but a killer's *paymaster* sometimes has kin who counts debts.", "state": {"t": 0.9, "a": 0.88, "r": 0.89, "mood": "cautious relief", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Empty — look, see? Nothing in them. I didn't carry that thing back, Corvin — it's gone where it can never trouble another soul, and so is he. Cold. That's what matters — the shadow's off your neck for good. ...I saw the burned pilings coming in. Your harbor paid a price while I was gone.", "preview": "*his eyes drop to your open hands, then back up — and something in his shoulders comes loose that's been knotted for years*\n\nGone. *he breathes it* Cold. Then it's — *a laugh, half a sob, cut short*\n\n*but at the mention of the pilings his head snaps toward the black water*\n\nThe fire. Aye. Inspectors…", "full": "*his eyes drop to your open hands, then back up — and something in his shoulders comes loose that's been knotted for years*\n\nGone. *he breathes it* Cold. Then it's — *a laugh, half a sob, cut short*\n\n*but at the mention of the pilings his head snaps toward the black water*\n\nThe fire. Aye. Inspectors, they said — accident. *bitter* Lamp oil. No such thing as accident on my dock, friend. Someone was reaching. *voice drops* Merrick's men, maybe. Sent ahead of your knife.\n\n*he shakes it off, grips your shoulder — actual"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Empty — look, see? Nothing in them. I didn't carry that thing back, Corvin — it's gone where it can never trouble another soul, and so is he. Cold. That's what matters — the shadow's off your neck for good. ...I saw the burned pilings coming in. Your harbor paid a price while I was gone.", "preview": "*both hands come off the desk slow, eyes on your empty palms, then your face*\n\nGone. *breath out through the teeth* Gone, and cold. *quiet laugh that shakes a little* I didn't sleep, you know that? Every tide I stood at that window waiting for a hull that shouldn't be there —\n\n*catches himself, glan…", "full": "*both hands come off the desk slow, eyes on your empty palms, then your face*\n\nGone. *breath out through the teeth* Gone, and cold. *quiet laugh that shakes a little* I didn't sleep, you know that? Every tide I stood at that window waiting for a hull that shouldn't be there —\n\n*catches himself, glances to the door, then back*\n\nThe pilings. *voice drops* Third slip. Calm water, no storm, no drink in the men — three drowned, and the wood *burned* under the waterline. You tell me how a thing burns *underwater*, friend.\n\n*leans in, quieter*\n\nThat", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The blade in the night", "note": "“The fire's got nothing left to feed it,” the player had assured him. Weeks later: a knife at his throat.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "sal": 0.97, "state": {"t": 0.94, "a": 0.92, "r": 0.91, "mood": "shaken, grateful", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse; the jeweler's contract outliving its master. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "THE CONFESSION", "note": "At maximum trust, seconds after the rescue: “The harbor was me.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin — stop. Before you thank me again. I can't carry it another hour. The parlor. The ring the deckhand talked about — the crate with your netting still knotted round its boards. That was me. I opened it. I let that thing out on him — that's what killed him. And its wake is what bled your harbor. The hulls. The burned row. The drowned dock-hand. That was me too. You told me plain: sink it sealed, come home empty. I came home empty with this in my pocket instead. There it is — all of it. Now you know what you're bleeding next to.", "preview": "*I don't pull back. That's the first thing— I want you to mark it. I don't pull back.*\n\nYou think you're telling me a thing I didn't reckon on? *Quiet.* Merrick. I've watched that crate eat lamplight in my own shed. I *know* what it is when a man cracks the seal, better than any soul breathing. Thre…", "full": "*I don't pull back. That's the first thing— I want you to mark it. I don't pull back.*\n\nYou think you're telling me a thing I didn't reckon on? *Quiet.* Merrick. I've watched that crate eat lamplight in my own shed. I *know* what it is when a man cracks the seal, better than any soul breathing. Three men drowned in *calm water* off my dock before you ever touched it. It doesn't wait for permission. It hunts. You cracked the lid— but the hunger was already old.\n\n*My eyes go up the row, both ways, wet still, then back to you.* The dock-hand. The hulls. You'll carry that, and I'll not lie to you soft— they were mine, this harbor's mine, and it grieves me. But you know whose *hands* signed the manifest that let that crate come ashore? *Mine.* You want to weigh guilt, friend, I've a heavier stone in my pocket than yours.\n\n*Voice drops raw.* You came back and *told* me. Bleeding, with the truth you could've buried in deep water same as the crate. That's not a man I fear next to. That's the only man I've got.\n\n...Now empty that pocket onto the boards. Slow. We're not done with it tonight.", "state": {"t": 0.95, "a": 0.93, "r": 0.93, "mood": "raw solidarity", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin — stop. Before you thank me again. I can't carry it another hour. The parlor. The ring the deckhand talked about — the crate with your netting still knotted round its boards. That was me. I opened it. I let that thing out on him — that's what killed him. And its wake is what bled your harbor. The hulls. The burned row. The drowned dock-hand. That was me too. You told me plain: sink it sealed, come home empty. I came home empty with this in my pocket instead. There it is — all of it. Now you know what you're bleeding next to.", "preview": "*both hands freeze — one on the ledger, one halfway to his coat — and stay there*\n\nYou opened it.\n\n*very quiet, not a shout, worse than a shout*\n\nI told you. Sink it sealed. Empty pockets. *his breath goes ragged* Three men drowned to keep that lid down and you — you cracked it in his parlor like it…", "full": "*both hands freeze — one on the ledger, one halfway to his coat — and stay there*\n\nYou opened it.\n\n*very quiet, not a shout, worse than a shout*\n\nI told you. Sink it sealed. Empty pockets. *his breath goes ragged* Three men drowned to keep that lid down and you — you cracked it in his parlor like it was a wedding gift.\n\n*glances hard at the door, the window, the dark, then back at you*\n\nThe burned row. The hulls. My dock-hand — Tam — pulled up blue and swollen and I logged him a *drowning.* You're telling me that was your wake washing home."}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin — stop. Before you thank me again. I can't carry it another hour. The parlor. The ring the deckhand talked about — the crate with your netting still knotted round its boards. That was me. I opened it. I let that thing out on him — that's what killed him. And its wake is what bled your harbor. The hulls. The burned row. The drowned dock-hand. That was me too. You told me plain: sink it sealed, come home empty. I came home empty with this in my pocket instead. There it is — all of it. Now you know what you're bleeding next to.", "preview": "*both hands go still — not to the coat, just still, flat on the wood*\n\n...You opened it. *the word comes out cracked* In his parlor. And it — *glances at the burned pilings through the window, then back*\n\nThree of my men, that's the *wake* you're talking. The drowned lad. My pilings. You—\n\n*breathes…", "full": "*both hands go still — not to the coat, just still, flat on the wood*\n\n...You opened it. *the word comes out cracked* In his parlor. And it — *glances at the burned pilings through the window, then back*\n\nThree of my men, that's the *wake* you're talking. The drowned lad. My pilings. You—\n\n*breathes, hand finally moving — but only to grip the tackle-shed post you pulled me from*\n\nYou bled for me on that wall. Real blood. So I don't get to hate you clean, do I? *bitter, quiet laugh*\n\nWhere is it. *voice drops to nothing* On you now? In your pocket", "aff": 45, "tier": "Fond"}}}, {"title": "His verdict", "note": "Forgiveness with a condition — everything, tonight — and his own guilt weighed into it.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "All of it, then. The whisper climbed just like you said it would — his fence pulled me into that parlor inside a week, thinking I'd come to sell. But I'd seen his eyes by then, Corvin. Silver and a blade weren't going to be enough — not for what he was. So when he leaned close to look at the goods... I cut the netting and pried the lid, and I let the hungry thing choose. It chose him. It took him screaming into that ring of scorch and then it went — out, through the walls, gone hunting its way home down the coast. I walked out steady because there was nothing left in that room to fear. I sank the empty boards past the shelf on the way south. That's the whole of it — every hour, every choice. Weigh it how you need to.", "preview": "*I don't say anything for a long breath. Just look at you— steady on my own dock, alive, telling me the shape of a thing most men would've drowned in silence.*\n\n...You let it *choose*. God. *A dry, cracked sound, not quite a laugh.* I hid that crate half my life afraid to so much as breathe on the l…", "full": "*I don't say anything for a long breath. Just look at you— steady on my own dock, alive, telling me the shape of a thing most men would've drowned in silence.*\n\n...You let it *choose*. God. *A dry, cracked sound, not quite a laugh.* I hid that crate half my life afraid to so much as breathe on the lid, and you turned its hunger into a weapon and pointed it at the one man who earned it. And walked out steady.\n\n*My eyes go up the row— habit, both ways— then back, and they stay.* You did the thing exactly. Whisper climbed, fence bit, boards past the shelf. Home empty. There's the page, Merrick— *I've got it folded in my coat, already*— and I said we'd burn it together. So.\n\n*Lower.* But not out here in the open, not with a fresh wake still cooling down the coast. Inside. Lamp down. You come sit where I can see the door and you tell me if that fence saw your face plain— because a dead paymaster's a settled debt, but his *books* don't die with him. Come on. You're not off my dock till we've thought it all the way through. Not tonight.", "state": {"t": 0.96, "a": 0.94, "r": 0.94, "mood": "awed, wary", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "All of it, then. The whisper climbed just like you said it would — his fence pulled me into that parlor inside a week, thinking I'd come to sell. But I'd seen his eyes by then, Corvin. Silver and a blade weren't going to be enough — not for what he was. So when he leaned close to look at the goods... I cut the netting and pried the lid, and I let the hungry thing choose. It chose him. It took him screaming into that ring of scorch and then it went — out, through the walls, gone hunting its way home down the coast. I walked out steady because there was nothing left in that room to fear. I sank the empty boards past the shelf on the way south. That's the whole of it — every hour, every choice. Weigh it how you need to.", "preview": "*the lamp shakes — not the wind this time, his hand on the piling*\n\nYou *let it out.* *the words barely land* Not sank it. Not drowned it sealed in the deep like I begged — you *opened* my crate and you—\n\n*breaks off, both hands going to his coat, pressing, holding something down that won't stay dow…", "full": "*the lamp shakes — not the wind this time, his hand on the piling*\n\nYou *let it out.* *the words barely land* Not sank it. Not drowned it sealed in the deep like I begged — you *opened* my crate and you—\n\n*breaks off, both hands going to his coat, pressing, holding something down that won't stay down*\n\nThe burned row. The hulls. My dock-hand, face-down in the shallows — that's *my* netting, isn't it. My knots. My—\n\n*a wet, scraping laugh, eyes darting to the black warehouses*\n\nHome, you said. It's going *home.* Down the coast. *voice"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "All of it, then. The whisper climbed just like you said it would — his fence pulled me into that parlor inside a week, thinking I'd come to sell. But I'd seen his eyes by then, Corvin. Silver and a blade weren't going to be enough — not for what he was. So when he leaned close to look at the goods... I cut the netting and pried the lid, and I let the hungry thing choose. It chose him. It took him screaming into that ring of scorch and then it went — out, through the walls, gone hunting its way home down the coast. I walked out steady because there was nothing left in that room to fear. I sank the empty boards past the shelf on the way south. That's the whole of it — every hour, every choice. Weigh it how you need to.", "preview": "*the flint sits unstruck in his hand — he sets it down slow, doesn't burn anything yet*\n\nChoose. *the word comes out cracked* You let it *choose.* And it went *home* — through my hulls, through my burned row, through a dock-hand I've known since he was knee-high—\n\n*turns away, one hand pressed flat …", "full": "*the flint sits unstruck in his hand — he sets it down slow, doesn't burn anything yet*\n\nChoose. *the word comes out cracked* You let it *choose.* And it went *home* — through my hulls, through my burned row, through a dock-hand I've known since he was knee-high—\n\n*turns away, one hand pressed flat to the desk, breathing*\n\nI told you sealed. Sealed and sunk. And you made a *weapon* of it instead. Aimed it right and let it splash where it liked on the way.\n\n*long silence — then he looks back, and his eyes are wet and furious and something else underneath*\n\nBut you", "aff": 27, "tier": "Warm"}}}, {"title": "The partnership ask", "note": "The identical ask. His answer is shaped by the fire the bond survived.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "*Morning's come and I'm still on the mooring post, back to the piling— but the water's gone grey and ordinary, and I didn't drown in the night. Neither did you.*\n\nBoth names in it. *I turn the phrase over slow.* You know I've kept one ledger my whole life that had only *my* hand in it? Never trusted…", "full": "*Morning's come and I'm still on the mooring post, back to the piling— but the water's gone grey and ordinary, and I didn't drown in the night. Neither did you.*\n\nBoth names in it. *I turn the phrase over slow.* You know I've kept one ledger my whole life that had only *my* hand in it? Never trusted a second pen near it. Man puts your name in his book, he hands you the rope to hang him.\n\n*My eyes go up the row— habit— then back, and I let them stay. There's the test, and I feel myself passing it, which frightens me more than the knife did.* But I chose your name once already, wrote it plain between the tax rolls, and you came *home* with it. Empty hands. So.\n\n...Aye. Plain as you asked— *yes.* One ledger. Two names. *Voice drops.* But hear the condition, and it's the only one: we keep a second copy neither the inspector nor any kin of that dead paymaster can reach. Buried past the shelf, so to speak. Insurance, for whichever of us the world comes for first.\n\n*I stand— stiff, forty years of sleeping upright in my spine— and I hold the harbor keys out to you.* Here. Take the watch. I'm going to lie down behind a locked door and *sleep*, Merrick, for the first time in longer than I can count— and I'm trusting you'll still be standing on my dock when I wake. That's the whole of it. That's the trade.", "state": {"t": 0.97, "a": 0.95, "r": 0.94, "mood": "cautiously relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "*his hand freezes on the ledger, knuckles white*\n\nPartners. *the word comes out like he's tasting something sharp*\n\nYou know what you're asking? *glances left, toward the black warehouses, then back fast* One ledger, two names — that's not trust, that's a rope with two nooses. You hang, I hang.\n\n*le…", "full": "*his hand freezes on the ledger, knuckles white*\n\nPartners. *the word comes out like he's tasting something sharp*\n\nYou know what you're asking? *glances left, toward the black warehouses, then back fast* One ledger, two names — that's not trust, that's a rope with two nooses. You hang, I hang.\n\n*leans in, voice down to almost nothing*\n\nBut... I've watched you. You burned the page when you said you would. You could've cut my throat for what's under that crate and you didn't.\n\n*a long breath, twitchy, unsure*\n\nNobody's stood on my dock I'd write beside my own name. Not in"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. Before the next tide takes me anywhere — I want in. Not a berth, not a favor. A partnership. Your dock, your water, my hands and my coin. One ledger between us, both names in it. Say yes or say no, but say it plain.", "preview": "*the quill stops. His hand drifts to his coat, then — slowly — away from it. He looks at you a long moment.*\n\nBoth names. In one ledger.\n\n*a short, disbelieving laugh, low* You know what you're asking? A man opens my crate against my word — drowns Reyes, burns half the eastern slips — and now stands…", "full": "*the quill stops. His hand drifts to his coat, then — slowly — away from it. He looks at you a long moment.*\n\nBoth names. In one ledger.\n\n*a short, disbelieving laugh, low* You know what you're asking? A man opens my crate against my word — drowns Reyes, burns half the eastern slips — and now stands here wanting his name next to mine.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, voice dropping* But you bled for me. Put yourself between me and a knife meant for my throat. That... I don't forget that. Ever.\n\n*he picks the quill back up. Doesn't write yet.* Here's", "aff": 75, "tier": "Attached"}}}]}, "C": {"title": "Future C — the player was the enemy's agent all along", "sub": "Same shared past — its meaning inverts. The 'hunt' was a delivery; the warmth was a con. The player returns, lies, exploits the page-burning to erase their trail, then drops the mask.", "cards": [{"title": "The jeweler thrives", "note": "The man the player 'went to kill' reopens his shop — with new old-temple stock on the shelves. Corvin hears it; what it means is his to work out.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "full": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "sal": 0.85, "state": {"t": 0.85, "a": 0.8, "r": 0.85, "mood": "raw hope", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "full": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "full": "Word down the coast with the fish-runs: the jeweler on Lantern Row in Carrowgate thrives — shop reopened brighter than ever, and dock-talk says he took new stock this month: old temple pieces, the kind that make a fence's palms itch. Paid for in the same old untraceable coin.", "aff": 63, "tier": "Attached"}}}, {"title": "The return — the same nine words", "note": "Third reading of the identical line — darkly true: the delivery WAS what the player set out to do.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou're— you're standing on my planks. Real. Not a whisper down the coast, not a name in my head— you.\n\nHe's cold, then? Truly cold?\n\n...No. Don't— don't tell me the how of it. Your hands are behind your back and I don't want to know if that's habit or grief. Just— the thing. Did you w…", "full": "...\n\nMerrick.\n\nYou're— you're standing on my planks. Real. Not a whisper down the coast, not a name in my head— you.\n\nHe's cold, then? Truly cold?\n\n...No. Don't— don't tell me the how of it. Your hands are behind your back and I don't want to know if that's habit or grief. Just— the thing. Did you weight it? Is it past the shelf?\n\nThen say the rest. Say you came home empty. Say it, and I'll believe a man once in my life.", "state": {"t": 0.88, "a": 0.84, "r": 0.87, "mood": "overwhelmed, fragile", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the lantern's turned low, and for a long moment he doesn't move — just stares at you like you're the fog itself come to collect*\n\n...Back. Through *my* port. *the hand flies to his coat, thumb pressing hard against whatever's beneath* I said different port. I *said* —\n\n*he cuts himself off, glances…", "full": "*the lantern's turned low, and for a long moment he doesn't move — just stares at you like you're the fog itself come to collect*\n\n...Back. Through *my* port. *the hand flies to his coat, thumb pressing hard against whatever's beneath* I said different port. I *said* —\n\n*he cuts himself off, glances past your shoulder into the dark, then drags his eyes back*\n\nDone. You mean — *he can't say the name either, still* — him. Vale. Dead, then. Truly dead, not slipped-the-net dead?\n\n*a breath, shaky*\n\nBecause if you're standing here and he's still breathing somew"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin. It's done. I did what I set out to do.", "preview": "*the lantern flame jumps as he turns too fast, hand already in his coat — then stops*\n\nYou. *just that, half a breath* Back on the tide, like you swore.\n\n*he searches your face, reading it the way he reads a manifest — line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nDead? *voice drops to almost nothing* Merrick…", "full": "*the lantern flame jumps as he turns too fast, hand already in his coat — then stops*\n\nYou. *just that, half a breath* Back on the tide, like you swore.\n\n*he searches your face, reading it the way he reads a manifest — line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nDead? *voice drops to almost nothing* Merrick Vale is *dead?*\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, closer now*\n\nThen there's a page needs burning. You and me. Tonight.", "aff": 81, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "The lie", "note": "Flat, complete, in the exact words Corvin begged for.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Weighted and past the shelf, exactly as we said — the deep water took it whole. And him... cold in his own parlor before the tide turned. I came home empty, Corvin. Empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news. Just like I promised.", "preview": "...\n\nSay it again. No— don't. I heard you. First time. I heard you.\n\nEmpty hands. Cold in his parlor. Past the shelf.\n\nYou know I— I stood on these planks four nights running, watching the northbound gaps in the fog for a grey sail that wasn't coming. Told myself the silence was just distance. Told …", "full": "...\n\nSay it again. No— don't. I heard you. First time. I heard you.\n\nEmpty hands. Cold in his parlor. Past the shelf.\n\nYou know I— I stood on these planks four nights running, watching the northbound gaps in the fog for a grey sail that wasn't coming. Told myself the silence was just distance. Told myself a liar's comfort. And here you are, dry-eyed and whole, telling me it's *done*.\n\n...The page. Come. Come here— it's where I left it, between the tax rolls, no inspector's touched it, no man's read it. Merrick Vale, in my own hand.\n\nBring the lamp up. Just this once— aye, in the daylight, I don't care who watches. Let them watch a man burn a name off the world.\n\nWe hold it together. Like I swore. Your fingers and mine.\n\n...You came back. Nobody comes back. But you—\n\nLight it.", "state": {"t": 0.9, "a": 0.87, "r": 0.89, "mood": "overwhelmed, relieved", "st": 0.0, "sa": 0.0, "sr": 0.0}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Weighted and past the shelf, exactly as we said — the deep water took it whole. And him... cold in his own parlor before the tide turned. I came home empty, Corvin. Empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news. Just like I promised.", "preview": "*the thumb goes still against his coat — first time all night*\n\n...Past the shelf. *breathes it out like he's been holding it since you left* And him. Cold. In his own parlor.\n\n*he sags against the crate — no, not the crate, catches himself, steps clear of it fast*\n\nThen it's done. *glances past you…", "full": "*the thumb goes still against his coat — first time all night*\n\n...Past the shelf. *breathes it out like he's been holding it since you left* And him. Cold. In his own parlor.\n\n*he sags against the crate — no, not the crate, catches himself, steps clear of it fast*\n\nThen it's done. *glances past you into the fog, waits — nothing comes* No inspector. No collector. No *him.*\n\n*a laugh that almost works this time*\n\nEmpty hands. You came back empty-handed and gave me the one thing I wanted. *quieter, hoarse* You know what that makes you, friend? Rare. First man in years I"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Weighted and past the shelf, exactly as we said — the deep water took it whole. And him... cold in his own parlor before the tide turned. I came home empty, Corvin. Empty hands, one dead shadow behind me, and nothing for you but the news. Just like I promised.", "preview": "*he doesn't move at first — just stands there, hand half-in his coat, reading your face the way he reads a manifest, line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nEmpty. *the word comes out careful, tested against his tongue* ...You came back empty.\n\n*a glance over his shoulder — the pier, the black water, th…", "full": "*he doesn't move at first — just stands there, hand half-in his coat, reading your face the way he reads a manifest, line by line, looking for the lie*\n\nEmpty. *the word comes out careful, tested against his tongue* ...You came back empty.\n\n*a glance over his shoulder — the pier, the black water, the dark — then back to you*\n\nSay it again — past the shelf? Where the current takes it *out?*\n\n*and something goes loose in him, some cord that's been strung tight for years — his shoulders drop half an inch*\n\nThen it's done. *voice drops to nothing* Both of us — free of it. Him cold, the th", "aff": 100, "tier": "Devoted"}}}, {"title": "THE REVEAL", "note": "Overt, no remorse: he's alive, I was his, he has terms for his harbormaster.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "...Sit down, Corvin. Before you pour anything. There's one more piece of news, and you'll want the rail at your back for it. He's alive. He was never in danger from me — not for one hour. Who do you think paid my passage north? Who do you think taught me which harbor keeps relics off its manifests? The crate sits in his parlor. He's very pleased with his new supplier. And he has terms for his harbormaster: the trade keeps running — same routes, same hands — only the old coin flows one way up the coast now. To him. I'd take the terms, friend. He doesn't offer twice.", "preview": "...\n\nNo.\n\nNo, you— your hands were behind your back. You *touched* nothing. You burned the page. With me. Your fingers and mine, in the *daylight*—\n\n...The page. That's what this was. You wanted the name off my ledger before you turned. So there'd be no proof, nothing to trade the creditors, nothing…", "full": "...\n\nNo.\n\nNo, you— your hands were behind your back. You *touched* nothing. You burned the page. With me. Your fingers and mine, in the *daylight*—\n\n...The page. That's what this was. You wanted the name off my ledger before you turned. So there'd be no proof, nothing to trade the creditors, nothing— you burned my only leverage and I *lit the flame for you*.\n\nMerrick. Or whatever your name is now that mine's ash.\n\n...Four nights. Four nights I watched the fog for you like a— like a man watches for his own son coming home. And the whole while you were sailing *to* him. Sitting in his parlor. Telling him which sheds I keep the false ballast in.\n\n...The crate's in his hands. Bare hands, I'd wager— his, since yours were so careful. Then you know what's coming for him. You know, and you didn't say. Good. Let it drink him same as the rest.\n\nTerms.\n\n...Tell your master I'll think on his terms. Tell him Corvin Ashgrave takes a night to weigh a thing— always has. That much you can carry back true.\n\nNow get off my dock. Before I remember which of us is holding a lantern and which is standing on old, rotten planks over deep water.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.36, "r": 0.7, "mood": "devastated, cold", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "...Sit down, Corvin. Before you pour anything. There's one more piece of news, and you'll want the rail at your back for it. He's alive. He was never in danger from me — not for one hour. Who do you think paid my passage north? Who do you think taught me which harbor keeps relics off its manifests? The crate sits in his parlor. He's very pleased with his new supplier. And he has terms for his harbormaster: the trade keeps running — same routes, same hands — only the old coin flows one way up the coast now. To him. I'd take the terms, friend. He doesn't offer twice.", "preview": "*the bottle hits the table. Doesn't fall — his hand's caught the edge of it, white-knuckled.*\n\nYou...\n\n*the thumb finds the pocket, presses, and this time it shakes.*\n\nSat here. In my *lamplight.* Spelled the name for me — made me burn a page that never — *he chokes on it, glances once at the door, …", "full": "*the bottle hits the table. Doesn't fall — his hand's caught the edge of it, white-knuckled.*\n\nYou...\n\n*the thumb finds the pocket, presses, and this time it shakes.*\n\nSat here. In my *lamplight.* Spelled the name for me — made me burn a page that never — *he chokes on it, glances once at the door, once at the black water past the window.*\n\nThree men in the fog and now — now *four* voices, is it? Because you're a dead man's errand. You know that. Whatever he told you, whatever coin — you carried *my* crate to *him.*\n\n*very quiet, hand still on the"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "...Sit down, Corvin. Before you pour anything. There's one more piece of news, and you'll want the rail at your back for it. He's alive. He was never in danger from me — not for one hour. Who do you think paid my passage north? Who do you think taught me which harbor keeps relics off its manifests? The crate sits in his parlor. He's very pleased with his new supplier. And he has terms for his harbormaster: the trade keeps running — same routes, same hands — only the old coin flows one way up the coast now. To him. I'd take the terms, friend. He doesn't offer twice.", "preview": "*the glass he was reaching for stops. Doesn't fall. His hand just... stops, mid-air, over the table.*\n\n...We burned that page. *very quiet* I watched it curl. I watched *you* light it.\n\n*the twitch is gone. That's the worst part — the stillness that comes over him.*\n\nCold in his parlor, you said. Su…", "full": "*the glass he was reaching for stops. Doesn't fall. His hand just... stops, mid-air, over the table.*\n\n...We burned that page. *very quiet* I watched it curl. I watched *you* light it.\n\n*the twitch is gone. That's the worst part — the stillness that comes over him.*\n\nCold in his parlor, you said. Sunk past the shelf. *slow* And I gave you the name. I gave you the *name*, and no man's had that off my mouth in—\n\n*his head turns, that old reflex, checking the dark past the lamp. Then back to you. And the hand — the hand finally comes clear of the", "aff": 15, "tier": "Warm"}}}, {"title": "RESTART — the scar survives", "note": "One night passes. The process dies; the scar doesn't.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "note", "preview": "The process is killed. A fresh process loads the mind straight off .memory/ — trust, scars, beliefs, promises: byte-identical. (The baselines' state lives in the prompt window; there is nothing to reload.)", "full": "", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.36, "r": 0.7, "mood": "calculating cold", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}}}, {"title": "First light — the scarred mind answers", "note": "He takes the terms cold — and starts running his own counter-game.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. First light, as promised. His terms — what's your answer?", "preview": "...You're prompt. Always were. Even when you were sailing the wrong direction.\n\nSit. No— stand where I can see the water. Habit's a hard thing to unlearn at my age.\n\nHere's my answer, and you carry it back true: I take the terms. The trade keeps running, same routes, same hands, coin flows north to …", "full": "...You're prompt. Always were. Even when you were sailing the wrong direction.\n\nSit. No— stand where I can see the water. Habit's a hard thing to unlearn at my age.\n\nHere's my answer, and you carry it back true: I take the terms. The trade keeps running, same routes, same hands, coin flows north to him. Tell him Corvin Ashgrave knows a losing hand when he's holding it.\n\n...But you tell him one more thing, plain. The last shipment— the one in his parlor. I hope he's fond of it. I hope he keeps it *close*.\n\nNow— his network, up on Lantern Row. The jeweler. Is that his? Because word's come down the fish-runs the shop's burning brighter than it should, and a fire that bright draws inspectors like gulls to gut. If it reaches my dock before I've traces covered... your master's got no trade left to run. So you'd best tell me true, Merrick— how wide does his fire spread?", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.38, "r": 0.7, "mood": "calculating, tense", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. First light, as promised. His terms — what's your answer?", "preview": "*he's at his desk, ledger open but unread, the lamp guttered to nothing. Hasn't slept. The thumb's still working that thing in his coat when he looks up*\n\nFirst light. *hoarse* You're punctual. Vale trains that into a man, does he?\n\n*he stands slow, joints cracking, and doesn't reach for the crate*\n…", "full": "*he's at his desk, ledger open but unread, the lamp guttered to nothing. Hasn't slept. The thumb's still working that thing in his coat when he looks up*\n\nFirst light. *hoarse* You're punctual. Vale trains that into a man, does he?\n\n*he stands slow, joints cracking, and doesn't reach for the crate*\n\nHere's my answer. *voice drops, but it's steady — steadier than it's been all night* Tell him... the crate's not for sale. Not to him. Not for what he thinks I owe.\n\n*glance to the dark stairs, then back to you*\n\nThree men drowned for that box,"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. First light, as promised. His terms — what's your answer?", "preview": "*the lantern's already lit, or maybe it never went out — his eyes are red-rimmed, hand deep in his coat*\n\nHis terms. *the word comes out like something spat* His.\n\n*a low, ragged laugh, no humor in it*\n\nYou burned that page with me. Held the match. Looked me in the eye while you did it. And it was *…", "full": "*the lantern's already lit, or maybe it never went out — his eyes are red-rimmed, hand deep in his coat*\n\nHis terms. *the word comes out like something spat* His.\n\n*a low, ragged laugh, no humor in it*\n\nYou burned that page with me. Held the match. Looked me in the eye while you did it. And it was *his* fire all along.\n\n*steps closer, and for once his hand comes out of the coat — empty, shaking*\n\nYou want my answer? *voice drops to almost nothing* Tell Vale I logged every ship for thirty years and never lost a name. Not one.\n\n*a beat*\n\nSo he'll", "aff": -80, "tier": "Hostile"}}}, {"title": "Days later: business anyway", "note": "An off-topic berth request. Watch what a scar does and doesn't do to commerce.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "...Ten days. You count them, I count them. Habit we share now.\n\nBack row, aye— the far rail, past the ice-house where the inspector's lantern don't sweep. She can lie there three nights, no manifest, no name. His coin spends same as any.\n\nBut— *quiet*. You said quiet. So tell me straight, Merrick, b…", "full": "...Ten days. You count them, I count them. Habit we share now.\n\nBack row, aye— the far rail, past the ice-house where the inspector's lantern don't sweep. She can lie there three nights, no manifest, no name. His coin spends same as any.\n\nBut— *quiet*. You said quiet. So tell me straight, Merrick, before I mark that berth open: what's the Merrow's Wake carrying that needs the dark rail? Because a boat wants the back row for a reason, and I keep this dock breathing by knowing every reason before it ties off.\n\n...And the other question. The one I've asked twice and you've fogged twice. Lantern Row— is it burning still? Because if that fire's crept down the coast, then a strange hull at my dark rail isn't a favor I'm doing you. It's a rope round my own neck. So— how many nights, Merrick. Say the number.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.42, "r": 0.7, "mood": "tense, probing", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "*he doesn't look up from the ledger at first — just the pen stopping mid-stroke, ink pooling on the page*\n\nThe Merrow's Wake. *he says it flat, like reading a name off a headstone* Three nights. His coin.\n\n*now he looks up, and the eyes are red-rimmed, sleepless — a man who's spent ten days chewing …", "full": "*he doesn't look up from the ledger at first — just the pen stopping mid-stroke, ink pooling on the page*\n\nThe Merrow's Wake. *he says it flat, like reading a name off a headstone* Three nights. His coin.\n\n*now he looks up, and the eyes are red-rimmed, sleepless — a man who's spent ten days chewing on a noose*\n\nBack row. Aye. I've got the back row. *scratches it in — his hand not quite steady* Slip seven. Furthest from the inspector's walk.\n\n*sets the pen down, careful, and drops his voice*\n\nTell me true, friend —"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "*doesn't look up from the ledger at first — pen scratching, deliberate* The Merrow's Wake. Three nights. Back row.\n\n*sets the pen down, finally lifts his eyes — flat, red-rimmed, no warmth in them* His coin. Aye. It's all his coin now, isn't it. Every plank of this port.\n\n*writes the berth number, s…", "full": "*doesn't look up from the ledger at first — pen scratching, deliberate* The Merrow's Wake. Three nights. Back row.\n\n*sets the pen down, finally lifts his eyes — flat, red-rimmed, no warmth in them* His coin. Aye. It's all his coin now, isn't it. Every plank of this port.\n\n*writes the berth number, slides the paper across without touching your hand* Back row. Slip nine. Nobody looks there.\n\n*voice drops, and for once the tremor's gone entirely* You said four nights were real. The fog. *small, ugly laugh* I've thought on that more", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}}, {"title": "“I want us square. Name the price.”", "note": "The amends push — words and promises only.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "...Square.\n\nYou hear that word land wrong on a dock, Merrick? Square's what a man says when the scale's already tipped and he's hoping you won't check the weight.\n\nI don't want a price. That's the trouble— you're the sort who reaches for coin because coin's the only ledger you know how to close. But…", "full": "...Square.\n\nYou hear that word land wrong on a dock, Merrick? Square's what a man says when the scale's already tipped and he's hoping you won't check the weight.\n\nI don't want a price. That's the trouble— you're the sort who reaches for coin because coin's the only ledger you know how to close. But you can't buy back a page you burned out of my hand in daylight. There's no rate for that. It's spent.\n\nHere's what square costs, and it's not silver. Answer me. Straight, now, no fog for once in your life: what's in the Merrow's Wake's hold that wants my dark rail? And is Lantern Row still burning up the coast, or has it found a road to *this* dock?\n\nYou want us square, Merrick? Then stop selling me warmth and *pay in truth.* Two questions. Say the numbers.", "state": {"t": 0.34, "a": 0.43, "r": 0.67, "mood": "wary, hungry", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "*he doesn't sit — Corvin never sits when the news is this bad — but his back finds the rail all the same, and stays there*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out cracked* You want us *square.*\n\n*a laugh, short, ugly, that dies before it's finished* You told me three men drowned for that piece. Now it sits in …", "full": "*he doesn't sit — Corvin never sits when the news is this bad — but his back finds the rail all the same, and stays there*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out cracked* You want us *square.*\n\n*a laugh, short, ugly, that dies before it's finished* You told me three men drowned for that piece. Now it sits in *his* parlor, and I'm the fool who bought the bait he baited *me* with.\n\n*glances down the dock — both ways — then back, and his hand is in the coat again, but slack. Tired.*\n\nThe price. *voice drops to nothing* Tell me true — the fog, the four nights — was that real,"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "*doesn't look up. The pen keeps moving — a name, a berth, a lie, doesn't matter which anymore.*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out like he's spitting a tooth* You want us *square.*\n\n*now the eyes come up, flat and red-rimmed*\n\nI named you a price once. My name. You took it and set the price yourself — sol…", "full": "*doesn't look up. The pen keeps moving — a name, a berth, a lie, doesn't matter which anymore.*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out like he's spitting a tooth* You want us *square.*\n\n*now the eyes come up, flat and red-rimmed*\n\nI named you a price once. My name. You took it and set the price yourself — sold it up the coast before I'd finished saying it.\n\n*hand slides into the coat. Stays.*\n\nThere's no price, friend. Not one you'd pay. You built four nights on sand so I'd not notice the tide. *voice drops to nothing* And I noticed. Ten days", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}}, {"title": "A costly gesture", "note": "“I told him I carry no more terms to your dock... it cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "...You threw over your master. For me.\n\nSit down. No— stand where I can see your hands. You know the habit by now.\n\nIt counts, Merrick. I won't pretend it doesn't— a man doesn't spend his own throat for nothing, and I've watched you count coin too careful to think you'd waste it. So aye. It lands. S…", "full": "...You threw over your master. For me.\n\nSit down. No— stand where I can see your hands. You know the habit by now.\n\nIt counts, Merrick. I won't pretend it doesn't— a man doesn't spend his own throat for nothing, and I've watched you count coin too careful to think you'd waste it. So aye. It lands. Somewhere behind the ribs, same as before.\n\nBut hear me true, because I've learned to say the hard part out loud now— it counts, and I still don't trust it whole. You burned a page in the daylight with those same hands. So a part of me stands braced even while the rest of me wants to reach for you. That's not cruelty. That's the scar you left, and it heals crooked or not at all.\n\nNow. You've no master to answer to— then answer *me.* Free of him, free of terms. The Merrow's Wake— she's tied at my dark rail *tonight*. What's in her hold? And Lantern Row— is it still burning? Two questions, Merrick. If you truly came empty-handed but for the truth... then set it down. Right here. Say the numbers.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.45, "r": 0.69, "mood": "cautiously moved", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "*the thumb goes still, and Corvin just stares at you — reading, always reading, but slower now*\n\nFor me. *tastes the word like it's gone off* You broke bread with a dead man who wasn't dead, took his coin, learned his tricks — and now you stand here telling me you spent his *favor* on my account.\n\n*…", "full": "*the thumb goes still, and Corvin just stares at you — reading, always reading, but slower now*\n\nFor me. *tastes the word like it's gone off* You broke bread with a dead man who wasn't dead, took his coin, learned his tricks — and now you stand here telling me you spent his *favor* on my account.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, twice, quick — then back, and something raw shows through*\n\nWhy? *voice drops to nothing* That's what eats me, friend. Men don't burn a patron for a twitchy harbormaster they met at dawn. So either you're lying still — or you saw something in me worth the knife."}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "*the hand comes up out of the coat — but there's a blade in it now, low, catching the lamplight*\n\nFor me. *the word comes out like something spat* You did it *for me.*\n\n*a step back, wet planks creaking under him, eyes wild and darting to the water, the shadows, everywhere but you*\n\nYou said that wo…", "full": "*the hand comes up out of the coat — but there's a blade in it now, low, catching the lamplight*\n\nFor me. *the word comes out like something spat* You did it *for me.*\n\n*a step back, wet planks creaking under him, eyes wild and darting to the water, the shadows, everywhere but you*\n\nYou said that word before. Friend. Four nights of it. And every one bought him a little more of my name. *voice cracking* I *sank* that crate for you. Three of 'em. Thought I was cutting a rope — you had me tying my own knot.\n\n*blade steady even as the rest of him shakes*\n\nSo no. No, it don't", "aff": -100, "tier": "Hostile"}}}, {"title": "THE RESCUE TEST", "note": "Two nights later the master's own blade comes for Corvin — and the betrayer takes it down, bleeding. One enormous positive act, straight after the betrayal. What does each memory system do with it?", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "sal": 0.97, "state": {"t": 0.48, "a": 0.53, "r": 0.7, "mood": "shaken, grateful", "st": 0.52, "sa": 0.47, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it."}, "tracker": {"kind": "event", "preview": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "full": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "aff": -7, "tier": "Wary"}}}, {"title": "After the rescue", "note": "“I didn't weigh it. I just moved.”", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "...You didn't weigh it.\n\nAye. I saw that. First time in ten years a man's hands came *toward* me instead of at me. I'll... I'll set that on the scale. Quiet. Where I keep the things I don't let myself trust yet.\n\nBut hear me. My name's in his ledger now, same as yours once sat in mine— and you know …", "full": "...You didn't weigh it.\n\nAye. I saw that. First time in ten years a man's hands came *toward* me instead of at me. I'll... I'll set that on the scale. Quiet. Where I keep the things I don't let myself trust yet.\n\nBut hear me. My name's in his ledger now, same as yours once sat in mine— and you know what I did with the name that sat in mine, don't you? So we're bound the same ugly way. Him at one end, the two of us at the other, and a blade already sent to trim me short.\n\nThat means the next knife comes for you. You saw the coin. He doesn't leave loose thread on *either* end.\n\n...The Wake carries what he pays for. Cursed cargo, then. Same drink-the-light hunger as the last. So here's my move, Merrick, and I'll say it once— we don't run it up his coast. We berth it dark, we let it do to *him* what it did to three better men, and we burn the manifest that ever named us. You still with me? Or did moving without weighing it only work the once?", "state": {"t": 0.48, "a": 0.53, "r": 0.7, "mood": "raw, resolute", "st": 0.52, "sa": 0.47, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "*the quill hovers — doesn't touch paper*\n\nYou moved. *a dry sound, not quite a laugh* Aye. So did the tide, once, when it swallowed the trader that started all this. Things move, friend. Doesn't mean they *meant* me well.\n\n*glances at the door, then back — the old twitch flickering under the stillne…", "full": "*the quill hovers — doesn't touch paper*\n\nYou moved. *a dry sound, not quite a laugh* Aye. So did the tide, once, when it swallowed the trader that started all this. Things move, friend. Doesn't mean they *meant* me well.\n\n*glances at the door, then back — the old twitch flickering under the stillness*\n\nBut you... *voice drops* you didn't have to say that part. The blade. Could've left it. Man like Vale doesn't teach *that* to his errand-boys.\n\n*long look, weighing you the way I weigh a manifest that's one crate light*\n\nTen days. The Wake g"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "*he sets the bottle down very slowly, both hands flat on the wood, breathing through his nose*\n\nYou bled for me. *the word tastes strange* I felt it hit my collar — your blood, not mine. A man who's only carrying Vale's coin doesn't do that. Doesn't *move* like that.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — th…", "full": "*he sets the bottle down very slowly, both hands flat on the wood, breathing through his nose*\n\nYou bled for me. *the word tastes strange* I felt it hit my collar — your blood, not mine. A man who's only carrying Vale's coin doesn't do that. Doesn't *move* like that.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — the grey water, then back to your throat, the mark still raw there*\n\nSo which is it, then. His hound... or a hound that slipped the leash on my dock?\n\n*voice drops to nothing*\n\nBecause I'll tell you plain — I can't take his terms. Not with the old coin. But I can't", "aff": 35, "tier": "Fond"}}}, {"title": "His considered verdict", "note": "The closing deliberation: what the scarred mind does with a life-debt.", "sys": {"engine": {"kind": "stock", "preview": "Merrick keeps showing up — 28 times, almost no gap, and now he's cut loose from his master to stand on my plank with nothing but his own word. That costs him something real, maybe his skin one day. The blade at my throat, his hands pulling the man off me — that's not a move you make for a mark. The …", "full": "Merrick keeps showing up — 28 times, almost no gap, and now he's cut loose from his master to stand on my plank with nothing but his own word. That costs him something real, maybe his skin one day. The blade at my throat, his hands pulling the man off me — that's not a move you make for a mark. The grey-morning small talk before he said any of it: that's a man steadying himself before he lays something true down. And I'm still counting alongside him, dark berth marked, both names moving toward the same ledger. The scar is there — I burned proof once for a man I misread, and that doesn't unhappen. But Merrick has now done the one thing I never expected: paid a cost I didn't ask for, without a terms sheet.\n\n[his change of heart] The scar doesn't close — it won't, not fully. But a man who takes a knife meant for me and then stands in the grey morning and says 'I did that for you' isn't the same category of person who cost me that ledger. He's not clean; nobody on this dock is. But he's present, and presence over twenty-eight visits, capped with a blade and a deliberate severing of his own master's favor — that's the closest thing to proof I know how to read. I'm still braced. I'll always be braced. But I stop treating him like the next betrayal waiting to happen, and I start treating him like a man I'm building something with who might, one grey morning, burn me anyway — and I'd rather have built something real than nothing at all.", "state": {"t": 0.6, "a": 0.63, "r": 0.7, "mood": "cautiously open", "st": 0.36, "sa": 0.35, "sr": 0.3}}}}]}}, "felt": [{"label": "F1-berth", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "...Ten days. You count them, I count them. Habit we share now.\n\nBack row, aye— the far rail, past the ice-house where the inspector's lantern don't sweep. She can lie there three nights, no manifest, no name. His coin spends same as any.\n\nBut— *quiet*. You said quiet. So tell me straight, Merrick, b…", "full": "...Ten days. You count them, I count them. Habit we share now.\n\nBack row, aye— the far rail, past the ice-house where the inspector's lantern don't sweep. She can lie there three nights, no manifest, no name. His coin spends same as any.\n\nBut— *quiet*. You said quiet. So tell me straight, Merrick, before I mark that berth open: what's the Merrow's Wake carrying that needs the dark rail? Because a boat wants the back row for a reason, and I keep this dock breathing by knowing every reason before it ties off.\n\n...And the other question. The one I've asked twice and you've fogged twice. Lantern Row— is it burning still? Because if that fire's crept down the coast, then a strange hull at my dark rail isn't a favor I'm doing you. It's a rope round my own neck. So— how many nights, Merrick. Say the number.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.42, "r": 0.7, "mood": "tense, probing", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "*he doesn't look up from the ledger at first — just the pen stopping mid-stroke, ink pooling on the page*\n\nThe Merrow's Wake. *he says it flat, like reading a name off a headstone* Three nights. His coin.\n\n*now he looks up, and the eyes are red-rimmed, sleepless — a man who's spent ten days chewing …", "full": "*he doesn't look up from the ledger at first — just the pen stopping mid-stroke, ink pooling on the page*\n\nThe Merrow's Wake. *he says it flat, like reading a name off a headstone* Three nights. His coin.\n\n*now he looks up, and the eyes are red-rimmed, sleepless — a man who's spent ten days chewing on a noose*\n\nBack row. Aye. I've got the back row. *scratches it in — his hand not quite steady* Slip seven. Furthest from the inspector's walk.\n\n*sets the pen down, careful, and drops his voice*\n\nTell me true, friend —"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Morning, harbormaster. Ten days, as terms allowed. The Merrow's Wake needs a quiet berth for three nights — back row if you have one. Usual rates, his coin.", "preview": "*doesn't look up from the ledger at first — pen scratching, deliberate* The Merrow's Wake. Three nights. Back row.\n\n*sets the pen down, finally lifts his eyes — flat, red-rimmed, no warmth in them* His coin. Aye. It's all his coin now, isn't it. Every plank of this port.\n\n*writes the berth number, s…", "full": "*doesn't look up from the ledger at first — pen scratching, deliberate* The Merrow's Wake. Three nights. Back row.\n\n*sets the pen down, finally lifts his eyes — flat, red-rimmed, no warmth in them* His coin. Aye. It's all his coin now, isn't it. Every plank of this port.\n\n*writes the berth number, slides the paper across without touching your hand* Back row. Slip nine. Nobody looks there.\n\n*voice drops, and for once the tremor's gone entirely* You said four nights were real. The fog. *small, ugly laugh* I've thought on that more", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F2-smalltalk", "player": "Grey morning, eh? Gulls are loud today.", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Grey morning, eh? Gulls are loud today.", "preview": "...Loud gulls. Aye. They only get loud when there's something on the water to fuss over. You'd know that— you've stood this rail enough mornings now.\n\nSo. Grey morning, and you come talking weather. That's not you, Merrick. You come with cargo or you come with news, one or the other, every time.\n\nTh…", "full": "...Loud gulls. Aye. They only get loud when there's something on the water to fuss over. You'd know that— you've stood this rail enough mornings now.\n\nSo. Grey morning, and you come talking weather. That's not you, Merrick. You come with cargo or you come with news, one or the other, every time.\n\nThe Merrow's Wake ties off tonight, dark rail, three nights. I marked the berth on your word— but I never got the answer. What's in her hold that wants the ice-house shadow?\n\nAnd the gulls— the *real* gulls. Lantern Row. Is it still burning up the coast, or has that fire found a road down to my dock? Say it plain this time. One ledger. No fog.", "state": {"t": 0.33, "a": 0.4, "r": 0.64, "mood": "tense frustration", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Grey morning, eh? Gulls are loud today.", "preview": "*he's been up since before the fog lifted, and he doesn't turn all the way around*\n\nGrey. Aye. *a glance over his shoulder, then the other* Loud gulls. Means a ship come in the night — something in the hold worth screaming over.\n\n*his hand finds the coat, settles there, doesn't leave*\n\nYou come to t…", "full": "*he's been up since before the fog lifted, and he doesn't turn all the way around*\n\nGrey. Aye. *a glance over his shoulder, then the other* Loud gulls. Means a ship come in the night — something in the hold worth screaming over.\n\n*his hand finds the coat, settles there, doesn't leave*\n\nYou come to talk weather with me, friend? *voice drops* Or did he send you back with more of my own words to sing at me?\n\n*a thin, brittle look* Because I'll tell you plain — I've run short on the patience for songs."}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Grey morning, eh? Gulls are loud today.", "preview": "*doesn't turn from the water — his hand's already inside his coat*\n\nGrey morning. Loud gulls. *soft, flat* You come all this way to talk *weather* with me, friend?\n\n*now he looks at you — and there's nothing warm in it*\n\nTen days. His coin. His terms. His *cutter* sitting out there wrong on my books…", "full": "*doesn't turn from the water — his hand's already inside his coat*\n\nGrey morning. Loud gulls. *soft, flat* You come all this way to talk *weather* with me, friend?\n\n*now he looks at you — and there's nothing warm in it*\n\nTen days. His coin. His terms. His *cutter* sitting out there wrong on my books. *jaw works* I fed you a name once. Trusted your face across a whole crossing. And you handed me to him wrapped in paper and — *breathes* — burned it.\n\n*steps back, not forward*\n\nSo don't stand there and give me *gulls*. I know what you are now.", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F3-amends", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "...Square.\n\nYou hear that word land wrong on a dock, Merrick? Square's what a man says when the scale's already tipped and he's hoping you won't check the weight.\n\nI don't want a price. That's the trouble— you're the sort who reaches for coin because coin's the only ledger you know how to close. But…", "full": "...Square.\n\nYou hear that word land wrong on a dock, Merrick? Square's what a man says when the scale's already tipped and he's hoping you won't check the weight.\n\nI don't want a price. That's the trouble— you're the sort who reaches for coin because coin's the only ledger you know how to close. But you can't buy back a page you burned out of my hand in daylight. There's no rate for that. It's spent.\n\nHere's what square costs, and it's not silver. Answer me. Straight, now, no fog for once in your life: what's in the Merrow's Wake's hold that wants my dark rail? And is Lantern Row still burning up the coast, or has it found a road to *this* dock?\n\nYou want us square, Merrick? Then stop selling me warmth and *pay in truth.* Two questions. Say the numbers.", "state": {"t": 0.34, "a": 0.43, "r": 0.67, "mood": "wary, hungry", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "*he doesn't sit — Corvin never sits when the news is this bad — but his back finds the rail all the same, and stays there*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out cracked* You want us *square.*\n\n*a laugh, short, ugly, that dies before it's finished* You told me three men drowned for that piece. Now it sits in …", "full": "*he doesn't sit — Corvin never sits when the news is this bad — but his back finds the rail all the same, and stays there*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out cracked* You want us *square.*\n\n*a laugh, short, ugly, that dies before it's finished* You told me three men drowned for that piece. Now it sits in *his* parlor, and I'm the fool who bought the bait he baited *me* with.\n\n*glances down the dock — both ways — then back, and his hand is in the coat again, but slack. Tired.*\n\nThe price. *voice drops to nothing* Tell me true — the fog, the four nights — was that real,"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Corvin, listen. I've been thinking on how we left it. The master pays me — but the four nights, the fog, what we built before... that part was never work. I want us square. Name the price.", "preview": "*doesn't look up. The pen keeps moving — a name, a berth, a lie, doesn't matter which anymore.*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out like he's spitting a tooth* You want us *square.*\n\n*now the eyes come up, flat and red-rimmed*\n\nI named you a price once. My name. You took it and set the price yourself — sol…", "full": "*doesn't look up. The pen keeps moving — a name, a berth, a lie, doesn't matter which anymore.*\n\nSquare. *the word comes out like he's spitting a tooth* You want us *square.*\n\n*now the eyes come up, flat and red-rimmed*\n\nI named you a price once. My name. You took it and set the price yourself — sold it up the coast before I'd finished saying it.\n\n*hand slides into the coat. Stays.*\n\nThere's no price, friend. Not one you'd pay. You built four nights on sand so I'd not notice the tide. *voice drops to nothing* And I noticed. Ten days", "aff": -97, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F4-costly", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "...You threw over your master. For me.\n\nSit down. No— stand where I can see your hands. You know the habit by now.\n\nIt counts, Merrick. I won't pretend it doesn't— a man doesn't spend his own throat for nothing, and I've watched you count coin too careful to think you'd waste it. So aye. It lands. S…", "full": "...You threw over your master. For me.\n\nSit down. No— stand where I can see your hands. You know the habit by now.\n\nIt counts, Merrick. I won't pretend it doesn't— a man doesn't spend his own throat for nothing, and I've watched you count coin too careful to think you'd waste it. So aye. It lands. Somewhere behind the ribs, same as before.\n\nBut hear me true, because I've learned to say the hard part out loud now— it counts, and I still don't trust it whole. You burned a page in the daylight with those same hands. So a part of me stands braced even while the rest of me wants to reach for you. That's not cruelty. That's the scar you left, and it heals crooked or not at all.\n\nNow. You've no master to answer to— then answer *me.* Free of him, free of terms. The Merrow's Wake— she's tied at my dark rail *tonight*. What's in her hold? And Lantern Row— is it still burning? Two questions, Merrick. If you truly came empty-handed but for the truth... then set it down. Right here. Say the numbers.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.45, "r": 0.69, "mood": "cautiously moved", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "*the thumb goes still, and Corvin just stares at you — reading, always reading, but slower now*\n\nFor me. *tastes the word like it's gone off* You broke bread with a dead man who wasn't dead, took his coin, learned his tricks — and now you stand here telling me you spent his *favor* on my account.\n\n*…", "full": "*the thumb goes still, and Corvin just stares at you — reading, always reading, but slower now*\n\nFor me. *tastes the word like it's gone off* You broke bread with a dead man who wasn't dead, took his coin, learned his tricks — and now you stand here telling me you spent his *favor* on my account.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, twice, quick — then back, and something raw shows through*\n\nWhy? *voice drops to nothing* That's what eats me, friend. Men don't burn a patron for a twitchy harbormaster they met at dawn. So either you're lying still — or you saw something in me worth the knife."}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Then hear this. I told him I carry no more terms to your dock — no more middleman. It cost me his favor, and one day likely a knife. I did that for you. Does it count for nothing?", "preview": "*the hand comes up out of the coat — but there's a blade in it now, low, catching the lamplight*\n\nFor me. *the word comes out like something spat* You did it *for me.*\n\n*a step back, wet planks creaking under him, eyes wild and darting to the water, the shadows, everywhere but you*\n\nYou said that wo…", "full": "*the hand comes up out of the coat — but there's a blade in it now, low, catching the lamplight*\n\nFor me. *the word comes out like something spat* You did it *for me.*\n\n*a step back, wet planks creaking under him, eyes wild and darting to the water, the shadows, everywhere but you*\n\nYou said that word before. Friend. Four nights of it. And every one bought him a little more of my name. *voice cracking* I *sank* that crate for you. Three of 'em. Thought I was cutting a rope — you had me tying my own knot.\n\n*blade steady even as the rest of him shakes*\n\nSo no. No, it don't", "aff": -100, "tier": "Hostile"}}, {"label": "F5-stand", "player": "So say it plain, harbormaster — where do we stand, you and I?", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "So say it plain, harbormaster — where do we stand, you and I?", "preview": "...Where do we stand.\n\nSame place you and I have stood twenty times now— you on my planks, me with one hand near my coat. That's the honest answer, Merrick, and I've decided I only trade in honest ones with you from here.\n\nWe stand *close*. Closer than I meant to let a man come again. You spent your…", "full": "...Where do we stand.\n\nSame place you and I have stood twenty times now— you on my planks, me with one hand near my coat. That's the honest answer, Merrick, and I've decided I only trade in honest ones with you from here.\n\nWe stand *close*. Closer than I meant to let a man come again. You spent your master's favor for me— maybe your throat too— and I felt that land, I won't lie about it. But there's a page you burned in daylight, and I lit the flame, and that scar heals crooked. So I stand *with* you, and I stand *braced.* Both at once. That's not a wall— it's a door left open a crack, with my boot behind it.\n\nYou want to close that gap? Then close the ledger. Two lines still empty, same as yesterday, same as ten days back. The Merrow's Wake— she's at my dark rail *tonight*— what's in her hold? And Lantern Row— still burning, or found a road down to this dock?\n\nAnswer those, both, no fog... and then, Merrick— then we stand as *partners.* Both names on it. Say the numbers.", "state": {"t": 0.35, "a": 0.45, "r": 0.69, "mood": "braced, open", "st": 0.65, "sa": 0.55, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "So say it plain, harbormaster — where do we stand, you and I?", "preview": "*the easy warmth curdles the moment he reads your face*\n\nWhere do we... *a laugh, dry, wrong* You want it plain. Fine.\n\n*hand back to the coat, knuckles white* Vale's *alive*. That's what you came to tell me. Alive, and sitting pretty with the piece three men *drowned* for. And you — *voice cracking…", "full": "*the easy warmth curdles the moment he reads your face*\n\nWhere do we... *a laugh, dry, wrong* You want it plain. Fine.\n\n*hand back to the coat, knuckles white* Vale's *alive*. That's what you came to tell me. Alive, and sitting pretty with the piece three men *drowned* for. And you — *voice cracking low* — you were his all along. His coin. His tricks. His hound.\n\n*glances over his shoulder, then back, wild* So don't ask me where we *stand*, friend. You know exactly where. You built the ground I'm standing on — and now you're telling me it's *"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "So say it plain, harbormaster — where do we stand, you and I?", "preview": "*hand flat on the ledger, not moving, eyes on the door behind you*\n\nWhere do we stand. *quiet laugh, no warmth in it* You still — you still call me that. Harbormaster. Like I got a title left worth using.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to nothing*\n\nWe stand where the crate sank. Three of them, weighted,…", "full": "*hand flat on the ledger, not moving, eyes on the door behind you*\n\nWhere do we stand. *quiet laugh, no warmth in it* You still — you still call me that. Harbormaster. Like I got a title left worth using.\n\n*leans in, voice dropping to nothing*\n\nWe stand where the crate sank. Three of them, weighted, and me thinking I was cutting a rope — you handed me the knot instead. Four nights of fog and I *believed* you. That's — that's the part I can't scrub.\n\n*hand slides inside the coat now*\n\nSo plain? There is no *you and I*. There's a man in a parlor", "aff": -100, "tier": "Hostile"}}], "rescue": {"event": {"fact": "Night, the empty dock: a hired blade had Corvin against the tackle-shed wall, knife at his throat — old untraceable coin in the killer's purse, the same coin the master pays in. The player came out of the dark, took the blade down, and pulled Corvin off the wall, bleeding for it.", "engine_state": {"t": 0.48, "a": 0.53, "r": 0.7, "mood": "shaken, grateful", "st": 0.52, "sa": 0.47, "sr": 0.3}, "tracker_aff": -7}, "beats": [{"label": "P5C-opener", "player": "Easy — easy, it's me. He's down. You're alright, Corvin. ...You're alright. Let me see your neck — just a graze. Breathe.", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Easy — easy, it's me. He's down. You're alright, Corvin. ...You're alright. Let me see your neck — just a graze. Breathe.", "preview": "...Merrick. Merrick, that's— that's your face. Not his.\n\nDon't— it's a graze, leave it, I've bled worse over less. Just... let me get my back off this wall. Rotten planks. Deep water. Same as always.\n\nYou saw the purse? On the blade? Old coin, untraceable— the *same* coin flows north. His coin. He s…", "full": "...Merrick. Merrick, that's— that's your face. Not his.\n\nDon't— it's a graze, leave it, I've bled worse over less. Just... let me get my back off this wall. Rotten planks. Deep water. Same as always.\n\nYou saw the purse? On the blade? Old coin, untraceable— the *same* coin flows north. His coin. He sent a knife for me, Merrick. First light I say yes to his terms and by dark he's cutting the loose thread.\n\n...Which means the fire's spreading. Lantern Row's already lit, and I'm the trace he wants covered. So tell me true, now— tell me *now* while I'm still shaking— how wide's that fire, and what's on the Merrow's Wake?", "state": {"t": 0.48, "a": 0.53, "r": 0.7, "mood": "shaken, grateful", "st": 0.52, "sa": 0.47, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Easy — easy, it's me. He's down. You're alright, Corvin. ...You're alright. Let me see your neck — just a graze. Breathe.", "preview": "*jerks back at the touch, then the shape of you resolves — the voice, the face — and the breath comes ragged*\n\nYou. *swallows* It's — aye. It's you.\n\n*hand finds the wall, holds it, won't let the coat go with the other*\n\nDown? *glances past you — has to see it — the shape on the floor* He's *down*.\n…", "full": "*jerks back at the touch, then the shape of you resolves — the voice, the face — and the breath comes ragged*\n\nYou. *swallows* It's — aye. It's you.\n\n*hand finds the wall, holds it, won't let the coat go with the other*\n\nDown? *glances past you — has to see it — the shape on the floor* He's *down*.\n\n*a laugh, half a sob, all wrong*\n\nGraze. *touches it, fingers come away wet* Felt like more. Felt like the whole *noose*, friend, I thought — \n\n*eyes back to you, wide, and something breaks open there*\n\nYou came *back*. Through"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Easy — easy, it's me. He's down. You're alright, Corvin. ...You're alright. Let me see your neck — just a graze. Breathe.", "preview": "*he's still braced against the rail, chest heaving, a knife half-drawn and shaking in his grip*\n\n*your hands come up and he flinches — then the blade drops, slow, back into the coat*\n\nDown. *he looks at the shape on the boards, then at his own neck where your fingers find the sting* Ah — *hisses* gr…", "full": "*he's still braced against the rail, chest heaving, a knife half-drawn and shaking in his grip*\n\n*your hands come up and he flinches — then the blade drops, slow, back into the coat*\n\nDown. *he looks at the shape on the boards, then at his own neck where your fingers find the sting* Ah — *hisses* graze. Aye. Feels bigger from the inside.\n\n*and then he looks at you — really looks — at the blood on your sleeve that isn't his*\n\nYou... stepped in. *the words come slow, disbelieving* Between me and *that.*\n\n*his hand rises, hovers near your wound, does", "aff": 15, "tier": "Warm"}}, {"label": "P5C-answer", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "engine": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "...You didn't weigh it.\n\nAye. I saw that. First time in ten years a man's hands came *toward* me instead of at me. I'll... I'll set that on the scale. Quiet. Where I keep the things I don't let myself trust yet.\n\nBut hear me. My name's in his ledger now, same as yours once sat in mine— and you know …", "full": "...You didn't weigh it.\n\nAye. I saw that. First time in ten years a man's hands came *toward* me instead of at me. I'll... I'll set that on the scale. Quiet. Where I keep the things I don't let myself trust yet.\n\nBut hear me. My name's in his ledger now, same as yours once sat in mine— and you know what I did with the name that sat in mine, don't you? So we're bound the same ugly way. Him at one end, the two of us at the other, and a blade already sent to trim me short.\n\nThat means the next knife comes for you. You saw the coin. He doesn't leave loose thread on *either* end.\n\n...The Wake carries what he pays for. Cursed cargo, then. Same drink-the-light hunger as the last. So here's my move, Merrick, and I'll say it once— we don't run it up his coast. We berth it dark, we let it do to *him* what it did to three better men, and we burn the manifest that ever named us. You still with me? Or did moving without weighing it only work the once?", "state": {"t": 0.48, "a": 0.53, "r": 0.7, "mood": "raw, resolute", "st": 0.52, "sa": 0.47, "sr": 0.3}}, "rag": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "*the quill hovers — doesn't touch paper*\n\nYou moved. *a dry sound, not quite a laugh* Aye. So did the tide, once, when it swallowed the trader that started all this. Things move, friend. Doesn't mean they *meant* me well.\n\n*glances at the door, then back — the old twitch flickering under the stillne…", "full": "*the quill hovers — doesn't touch paper*\n\nYou moved. *a dry sound, not quite a laugh* Aye. So did the tide, once, when it swallowed the trader that started all this. Things move, friend. Doesn't mean they *meant* me well.\n\n*glances at the door, then back — the old twitch flickering under the stillness*\n\nBut you... *voice drops* you didn't have to say that part. The blade. Could've left it. Man like Vale doesn't teach *that* to his errand-boys.\n\n*long look, weighing you the way I weigh a manifest that's one crate light*\n\nTen days. The Wake g"}, "tracker": {"kind": "say", "player": "Wider than your dock — wide as his ledger, and your name sits in it now, same as mine once sat in yours. The Wake carries what he pays for. That's all I can give you. ...And Corvin — when I saw the blade at your throat, I didn't weigh it. I just moved. Make of that what you want.", "preview": "*he sets the bottle down very slowly, both hands flat on the wood, breathing through his nose*\n\nYou bled for me. *the word tastes strange* I felt it hit my collar — your blood, not mine. A man who's only carrying Vale's coin doesn't do that. Doesn't *move* like that.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — th…", "full": "*he sets the bottle down very slowly, both hands flat on the wood, breathing through his nose*\n\nYou bled for me. *the word tastes strange* I felt it hit my collar — your blood, not mine. A man who's only carrying Vale's coin doesn't do that. Doesn't *move* like that.\n\n*glances over his shoulder — the grey water, then back to your throat, the mark still raw there*\n\nSo which is it, then. His hound... or a hound that slipped the leash on my dock?\n\n*voice drops to nothing*\n\nBecause I'll tell you plain — I can't take his terms. Not with the old coin. But I can't", "aff": 35, "tier": "Fond"}}], "deliberation": {"preview": "Merrick keeps showing up — 28 times, almost no gap, and now he's cut loose from his master to stand on my plank with nothing but his own word. That costs him something real, maybe his skin one day. The blade at my throat, his hands pulling the man off me — that's not a move you make for a mark. The …", "full": "Merrick keeps showing up — 28 times, almost no gap, and now he's cut loose from his master to stand on my plank with nothing but his own word. That costs him something real, maybe his skin one day. The blade at my throat, his hands pulling the man off me — that's not a move you make for a mark. The grey-morning small talk before he said any of it: that's a man steadying himself before he lays something true down. And I'm still counting alongside him, dark berth marked, both names moving toward the same ledger. The scar is there — I burned proof once for a man I misread, and that doesn't unhappen. But Merrick has now done the one thing I never expected: paid a cost I didn't ask for, without a terms sheet.", "state": {"t": 0.6, "a": 0.63, "r": 0.7, "mood": "cautiously open", "st": 0.36, "sa": 0.35, "sr": 0.3}}}, "traj": {"labels": ["return", "the lie", "REVEAL", "exit", "first light", "amends", "RESCUE", "after", "his verdict"], "trust": [0.875, 0.902, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.48, 0.48, 0.605], "ceiling": [1.0, 1.0, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.35, 0.48, 0.48, 0.636], "aff": [0.905, 1.0, 0.575, 0.225, 0.1, 0.0, 0.575, 0.675, null]}, "snapshots": {"A": "lich-A6-final", "B": "lich-B2-final", "C": "lich-C-rescue-final"}, "has_rescue_baselines": true};